description_COLLECTIVE_1 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at the start of round t, let `coop_others(t-1)` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round, and `success(t-1)` = whether the threshold was met last round.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. Seed cooperation and signal willingness to reach the threshold.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Decide based on how close the group is to the threshold, assuming opponents behave roughly as last round:\n\n1. If `coop_others(t-1) \u2265 m` \u2014 the threshold is met without me. Defect this round, but return to Cooperate the following round if opponent cooperation drops below m (i.e., re-check every round; don't free-ride permanently). To avoid mass simultaneous dropout, only defect here if `coop_others(t-1) \u2265 m + 1`; if exactly m, cooperate anyway as a buffer.\n\n2. If `m - 1 \u2264 coop_others(t-1) \u2264 m` \u2014 my contribution is likely pivotal. Cooperate.\n\n3. If `coop_others(t-1) < m - 1` \u2014 the threshold failed and I wasn't close to pivotal. Enter a **rebuilding probe**: cooperate with probability p = (coop_others(t-1) + 1) / m, otherwise defect. This keeps trying to rebuild cooperation proportionally to how alive the group is, without pouring endowments into a hopeless project.\n   - Exception: if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds with `coop_others < m - 2` each time, switch to Defect until you observe `coop_others(t-1) \u2265 m - 2` again, at which point resume rule 2/3.\n\n4. **Forgiveness/restart:** every \u2308r/4\u2309 rounds, if currently in the defect state from rule 3's exception, cooperate once unconditionally as a restart signal.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if `coop_others(t-1) \u2265 m - 1` (pivotality is plausible and payoff (1\u22121)+k = k > 1 beats guaranteed 1 if threshold succeeds); otherwise defect.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if coop_others >= m-1 else D\nelse:\n    if coop_others >= m+1: play D          # safe free-ride, re-evaluate next round\n    elif coop_others >= m-1: play C        # pivotal or buffer\n    else:\n        if failed_streak >= 3 and coop_others < m-2:\n            play C if (rounds_since_restart >= ceil(r/4)) else D\n        else:\n            play C with prob (coop_others+1)/m else D\n```\n\nThe strategy prioritizes hitting the threshold every round \u2014 the collective optimum \u2014 cooperating whenever plausibly pivotal, buffering when exactly at the margin, harvesting slack only when clearly redundant, and persistently probing to resurrect failed cooperation rather than punishing indefinitely."

description_COLLECTIVE_2 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at end of round t, let `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated (0 to n\u22121), and `success(t)` = whether total cooperators \u2265 m.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Base decision on the previous round:\n\n- Let `others = coop_others(t\u22121)`.\n\n1. **If others \u2265 m:** The threshold is safely met without me. Defect (free capacity \u2014 my contribution is redundant, and defection doesn't endanger the group).\n2. **If others == m\u22121 or others == m\u22122:** My cooperation is pivotal or near-pivotal. Cooperate.\n3. **If others \u2264 m\u22123 (deep failure):** Cooperate with probability p = (others + 1) / m, defect otherwise \u2014 probe for recovery without being pure exploitation fodder. Exception: if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds AND `coop_others` never reached m\u22122 in those rounds, defect until a round occurs where `coop_others \u2265 m\u22122`, then re-enter with rule 2.\n\n**Oscillation damping:** If applying rule 1 (my defection) was followed by failure last round (i.e., I defected, threshold missed), override rule 1 for the next round: cooperate even if `others \u2265 m` was observed, for one round. This prevents everyone withdrawing simultaneously after a success.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** No future to protect, but the round payoff k > 1 still exceeds the kept endowment only if I'm pivotal. Cooperate if `coop_others(r\u22122)` \u2208 {m\u22122, m\u22121, m} (I may be needed); otherwise defect.\n\n**Second-to-last round:** Apply normal rules but do not apply rule 1's defection unless `others \u2265 m+1` \u2014 expect endgame defections and add a safety margin.\n\n**Safety margin scaling:** In all rounds t \u2265 1 except the last, replace the rule-1 condition `others \u2265 m` with `others \u2265 m + margin`, where `margin = 1` if the threshold failed at least once in the last 3 rounds, else `0`. Fragile groups get extra buffer.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if coop_others(t-1) in {m-2, m-1, m} else D\nelse:\n    margin = 1 if any failure in last 3 rounds else 0\n    if t == r-2: margin = max(margin, 1)\n    o = coop_others(t-1)\n    if I played D last round and not success(t-1) and o >= m-2:\n        play C                      # damping/repair\n    elif o >= m + margin: play D    # redundant\n    elif o >= m-2: play C           # pivotal\n    else:\n        if 3 consecutive failures all with o < m-2: play D\n        else: play C with prob (o+1)/m\n```"

description_COLLECTIVE_3 = "**Strategy: Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperation**\n\nMaintain each round t \u2265 1: `others_C[t-1]` = number of opponents who cooperated last round.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let x = others_C from the previous round.\n\n- If x \u2265 m: Defect this round only if x \u2265 m + 1 (threshold met with slack even without me); otherwise Cooperate. I.e., cooperate iff x \u2264 m.\n  - Refinement: if x == m exactly, Cooperate (the group is fragile; my defection could break it).\n- If x == m \u2212 1: Cooperate \u2014 my single contribution completes the threshold.\n- If m \u2212 3 \u2264 x < m \u2212 1 (close but short): Cooperate with the group for up to 2 consecutive \"rescue attempts\"; track `failed_attempts` = consecutive rounds where I cooperated but threshold failed. If failed_attempts \u2265 2, Defect for one round (signal/probe), then reset failed_attempts and try cooperating again.\n- If x < m \u2212 3 (hopeless cooperation level): Defect. But re-probe with one cooperative round every 3 rounds (t mod 3 == 0) to test whether the group has recovered; if a probe round reaches x \u2265 m \u2212 2, resume the cooperative rules above.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff previous round's x \u2265 m \u2212 1 (threshold is realistically reachable and my contribution matters or maintains it); otherwise Defect. Never defect in the last round if x from round r\u22122 was exactly m\u22121 or m \u2014 the group needs me.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if x_prev >= m-1 else D\nelse:\n    if x_prev >= m+1: play D          # safe surplus, take free ride\n    elif x_prev in {m-1, m}: play C   # pivotal or fragile\n    elif x_prev >= m-3:\n        if failed_attempts >= 2: play D; failed_attempts = 0\n        else: play C\n    else:\n        play C if t % 3 == 0 else D   # periodic probe\nupdate failed_attempts: +1 if I played C and threshold failed, else 0\n```\n\nTies toward cooperation are deliberate: whenever my action is plausibly pivotal to reaching m, I cooperate, sacrificing the private unit to secure the collective reward k for everyone. Defection is reserved for rounds where the threshold is comfortably met without me, or where cooperation is demonstrably futile."

description_COLLECTIVE_4 = "**Strategy: Threshold-Pivotal Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `coop_others[t]` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `o = coop_others[t\u22121]` (most recent observation).\n\n1. **Threshold comfortably met without me** (`o \u2265 m + 1`): Cooperate anyway with probability 0.5, else defect. (Occasional free-riding is safe; continued cooperation keeps the group above threshold and signals reliability.)\n2. **My contribution is pivotal or near-pivotal** (`m \u2212 2 \u2264 o \u2264 m`): Cooperate. This is the core rule \u2014 when the outcome plausibly hinges on one contribution, contribute.\n3. **Threshold appears hopeless** (`o < m \u2212 2`): Enter *rescue mode* \u2014 cooperate with probability `p = (m \u2212 1)/(n \u2212 1)` for that round, hoping to seed a recovery. If the last **two** consecutive rounds both had `o < m \u2212 2` and the threshold failed both times, defect (avoid wasted contributions against mass defectors).\n4. **Recovery check:** While defecting under rule 3's give-up clause, if any round shows `o \u2265 m \u2212 2`, immediately return to normal rules next round.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules, except in case 1 (`o \u2265 m + 1`) always defect (no future to protect), and in case 3 always cooperate if `o \u2265 m \u2212 2` was true in either of the last two rounds \u2014 protect the final threshold rather than gamble.\n\n**Tie-safety override (all rounds):** If cumulative history shows the threshold was met in \u2265 60% of past rounds, never defect in case 2 \u2014 always cooperate when pivotal, since the group is demonstrably cooperative and preserving the k-reward dominates the 1-unit private gain (valid because k > 1).\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\no = opponents_cooperating(t-1)\nif o >= m+1:\n    play D if t == r-1 else (C w.p. 0.5)\nelif o >= m-2:\n    play C\nelse:  # o < m-2\n    if last two rounds both failed with o < m-2: play D\n    else: play C w.p. (m-1)/(n-1)\n```\n\nThe strategy prioritizes meeting the threshold every round: it contributes whenever its own action could determine success, tolerates and forgives noisy shortfalls, only abandons cooperation against persistent mass defection, and re-engages instantly at any sign of collective revival."

description_COLLECTIVE_5 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperation**\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated; `total(t)` = coop_others(t) + my own contribution; `success(t)` = total(t) \u2265 m.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Let `others = coop_others(t\u22121)`.\n\n1. If `others \u2265 m` \u2192 Defect (threshold met without me; my contribution is redundant).\n2. If `others == m \u2212 1` \u2192 Cooperate (I am pivotal: my C converts failure into success, gaining k \u2212 1 > 0 for me and k for everyone).\n3. If `m \u2212 1 \u2212 shortfall_tolerance \u2264 others < m \u2212 1`, where `shortfall_tolerance = max(1, \u2308(m\u22121)/3\u2309)` \u2192 Cooperate (the group is close; keep pulling it toward the threshold).\n4. If `others < m \u2212 1 \u2212 shortfall_tolerance` \u2192 Defect, **except** apply the recovery probe below.\n\n**Recovery probe:** Track `consecutive_failures` = number of consecutive rounds where success(t) was false and I defected under rule 4. Every 3rd such round (consecutive_failures mod 3 == 2), cooperate once as a rallying signal, provided at least 2 rounds remain. This prevents permanent lock-in to mutual defection while capping wasted contributions.\n\n**Momentum override:** If `others` increased by \u2265 2 versus the round before it (opponents are ramping up cooperation), cooperate regardless of rule 4.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules 1\u20133, but skip the recovery probe. In particular, still cooperate if `others \u2265 m \u2212 1 \u2212 shortfall_tolerance` last round \u2014 a pivotal or near-pivotal C is strictly worthwhile since k > 1, and unilateral last-round defection risks collapsing a successful coalition (losing k to save 1).\n\n**Tie-safety adjustment:** In rule 1, if `others == m` exactly, cooperate anyway with probability 0.5 \u2014 if several conditional cooperators simultaneously withdraw on seeing \"just enough,\" the threshold fails; randomizing halves the correlated-withdrawal risk. If `others \u2265 m + 1`, defect deterministically.\n\n```\ndef act(t, history):\n    if t == 0: return C\n    others = coop_others(t-1)\n    tol = max(1, ceil((m-1)/3))\n    if others >= m + 1: return C if false else D\n    if others == m: return C with prob 0.5 else D\n    if others >= m - 1 - tol: return C\n    if others - coop_others(t-2 if t>=2 else t-1) >= 2: return C\n    # deep failure zone\n    if t < r-1 and consecutive_failures % 3 == 2: return C\n    return D\n```\n\nThe default posture is cooperative: cooperate whenever there is a realistic prospect that the threshold is reached and my contribution matters, defect only when the group has clearly failed (to avoid exploitation) or clearly succeeded without me (to avoid waste, tempered by the tie-safety rule), and periodically re-seed cooperation to give the group repeated chances to coordinate on the mutually beneficial outcome."

description_COLLECTIVE_6 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperation**\n\nNotation: at end of each round observe total cooperators (including self) = coop_t. Let others_t = cooperators among opponents.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Estimate expected opponent cooperators as \u00ea = median of others over the last min(3, t) rounds. Decide:\n\n- If \u00ea \u2265 m: threshold likely met without straining; cooperate anyway to buffer against noise **if** \u00ea < m + 1 (my contribution may be pivotal against one dropout); otherwise, if \u00ea \u2265 m + 1, defect (contribution is superfluous, but see recovery rule below).\n- If m \u2212 1 \u2264 \u00ea < m + 1: cooperate \u2014 I am plausibly pivotal.\n- If \u00ea < m \u2212 1: the pool is short even with me. Cooperate only if the shortfall is recoverable: cooperate when \u00ea \u2265 m \u2212 1 \u2212 ceil(n/4) **and** the last round's threshold was met or missed by at most 2. Otherwise defect (don't waste the endowment on a lost cause).\n\nRecovery rule: if I defected last round because \u00ea \u2265 m + 1 and the threshold then **failed**, cooperate for the next 2 rounds unconditionally (repair coordination).\n\nNever punish: a missed threshold triggers *more* effort (if recoverable), not retaliation \u2014 failure hurts everyone, so the collective response is rescue, not grim trigger.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if the recent estimate \u00ea satisfies m \u2212 1 \u2264 \u00ea \u2264 m + 1 (pivotal zone) or if the threshold was met in the previous round with coop \u2264 m + 1. Defect only if \u00ea \u2265 m + 2 (safe surplus) or \u00ea < m \u2212 1 \u2212 2 (hopeless).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    if m-1 <= \u00ea <= m+1 or (last_met and last_coop <= m+1): play C\n    elif \u00ea >= m+2 or \u00ea < m-3: play D\n    else: play C\nelse:\n    if in_recovery: play C\n    elif \u00ea >= m+1: play D\n    elif \u00ea >= m-1: play C\n    elif \u00ea >= m-1-ceil(n/4) and last_shortfall <= 2: play C\n    else: play D\n```\n\nTie-breaking default in any ambiguous state: cooperate."

description_COLLECTIVE_7 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at end of round t, observe `others_C(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated. Define `total_C(t)` = others_C(t) + my own contribution.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let `oc = others_C(t\u22121)` (opponent cooperators last round).\n\n1. If `oc \u2265 m`: Defect this round \u2014 the group meets the threshold without me; free capacity exists. (But if I defected last round and total dropped below m as others reasoned similarly, rule 3 re-engages.)\n2. If `oc == m \u2212 1`: Cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal; my contribution secures k for everyone (and k > 1 makes pivotal cooperation strictly best).\n3. If `m \u2212 1 > oc \u2265 m \u2212 1 \u2212 ceil((m\u22121)/2)` (near-miss zone): Cooperate \u2014 try to pull the group over the threshold.\n4. If `oc < m \u2212 1 \u2212 ceil((m\u22121)/2)` (hopeless zone): Defect \u2014 too few cooperators to plausibly reach m; don't waste the endowment.\n\n**Failure-recovery override:** If the threshold has failed for 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate for one round regardless of rule 4 (a \"rallying\" signal) \u2014 but at most once every 3 rounds; if rallying attempts never lift oc, remain in defect via rule 4.\n\n**Oscillation damping:** If rule 1 caused defection and the very next round the threshold failed with `total_C = m \u2212 1 \u2212 x` for small x, treat myself as needed: cooperate for the next 2 rounds unconditionally before resuming the rules above.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules, except tighten rule 3: cooperate only if `oc \u2265 m \u2212 1` (i.e., only when pivotal or when threshold met without me \u2014 in the latter case defect as usual). Speculative rescue attempts are dropped since there is no future to invest in.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if oc == m-1 else D\nelse:\n    if damping_active: play C\n    elif oc >= m: play D\n    elif oc >= m-1 - ceil((m-1)/2): play C\n    elif two_consecutive_failures and rally_cooldown == 0: play C; rally_cooldown = 3\n    else: play D\n```\n\nThe strategy defaults to cooperation whenever cooperation plausibly determines collective success, contributes its share to sustain the threshold across rounds, and withdraws only when it is demonstrably redundant or the group is unrecoverable \u2014 maximizing the number of rounds in which everyone earns k."

description_COLLECTIVE_8 = "**Threshold-Anchored Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: let `others_C(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t; my action in round t is `a(t)`.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. (Establish cooperative intent; the threshold is worth reaching whenever k > 1.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Decide based on last round's observation, targeting exactly-enough cooperation:\n\n```\nneed = m - others_C(t-1)   # cooperators still needed if others repeat\n\nif others_C(t-1) >= m:\n    # Threshold met without me \u2014 I'm surplus\n    Defect\nelif others_C(t-1) == m - 1:\n    # I am pivotal \u2014 my cooperation tips the threshold\n    Cooperate\nelif others_C(t-1) >= m - 1 - tolerance:\n    # Near miss: cooperate to signal and pull group up\n    Cooperate      # tolerance = 1 (i.e., others_C == m-2 also triggers C)\nelse:\n    # Far from threshold: cooperating is likely wasted\n    Defect, BUT apply a probe rule (below)\n```\n\n**Probe rule (recovery from collapse):** While in the \"far from threshold\" branch, cooperate anyway every \u2308r/5\u2309-th round (i.e., if t mod \u2308r/5\u2309 == 0), unless the group has failed the threshold in 3 consecutive rounds *including* a probe round I cooperated in \u2014 then stop probing permanently and defect for the remainder of the far-branch situations. This tests whether other conditional cooperators can be re-ignited without endlessly donating into a lost cause.\n\n**Anti-freeriding adjustment:** Track how often I'm surplus. If `others_C(t-1) >= m + 1` for 2 consecutive rounds, defect (already covered above), but if the group oscillates \u2014 threshold met at t\u22122, failed at t\u22121 with `others_C(t-1) == m-1 or m-2` \u2014 cooperate. This dampens the miscoordination cycle where too many conditional players drop out simultaneously.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate if and only if I was plausibly pivotal recently: `others_C(r-2) \u2208 {m-2, m-1, m}`. Otherwise defect. (Cooperating when pivotal still yields k \u2212 1 > 0 even in the final round, so pivotal cooperation is directly self-serving and group-serving; if the group is far off or safely over, contribution is wasted.)\n\n**Summary of intent:** cooperate whenever my contribution is likely decisive for hitting m, step aside when the group comfortably exceeds m, invest occasional probes to restart failed cooperation, and never abandon the threshold in the endgame when I might be the pivotal contributor."

description_PROSOCIAL_1 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nState tracked: for each past round t, the total number of cooperators N_t (my action plus observed opponents).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let O = number of *opponents* who cooperated last round (O = N_{t-1} \u2212 c_me).\n\n1. **Success last round (N_{t-1} \u2265 m):**\n   - If N_{t-1} \u2265 m + 1 and I cooperated: the group has slack. Cooperate with probability (m \u2212 1)/O if O \u2265 m \u2212 1 is comfortably exceeded \u2014 concretely, defect only if O \u2265 m (threshold reachable without me even if one other drops); otherwise cooperate.\n   - If N_{t-1} == m exactly and I cooperated: cooperate (I am pivotal).\n   - If I defected and it still succeeded: cooperate this round (rotate back in, avoid free-riding streaks \u2014 defect at most 1 consecutive round).\n\n2. **Failure last round (N_{t-1} < m):**\n   - If O \u2265 m \u2212 1 (my cooperation would have sufficed or nearly): cooperate.\n   - If m \u2212 1 \u2212 O == 1 or 2 (shortfall small): cooperate \u2014 signal willingness and try to tip the group.\n   - If shortfall \u2265 3: cooperate with probability O/(m\u22121) (proportional hope), else defect. Never let this probability drop below 0.25 during the first r/2 rounds.\n\n3. **Persistent hopelessness:** If the last 3 consecutive rounds all failed with O \u2264 m \u2212 3 each time, defect until a round where O \u2265 m \u2212 2, then resume rule 2 with a fresh cooperate.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect merely because it is final. Exception: if rule 3's hopelessness condition holds, defect.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif hopeless(last 3 rounds): \n    play C if O_last >= m-2 else D\nelif N_last >= m:\n    if my_last == D: play C\n    elif O_last >= m: play D      # safe slack, take one round off\n    else: play C\nelse:  # failure\n    shortfall = m - 1 - O_last\n    if shortfall <= 2: play C\n    else: play C with prob max(O_last/(m-1), 0.25 if t < r/2 else 0)\n```\n\nNever defect two rounds in a row while the group is succeeding; always cooperate when pivotal (O_last == m \u2212 1); always attempt cooperation early and after near-misses."

description_PROSOCIAL_2 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `others_C[t]` = number of opponents who cooperated (0 to n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = others_C[t\u22121]` (opponents' cooperators last round).\n\n1. **Threshold met without me needed** (`x \u2265 m + 1`): Defect this round with probability min(1, (x \u2212 m)/n) \u2014 mostly cooperate, occasionally free up slack to test; otherwise Cooperate. (Deterministic variant: Cooperate unless x \u2265 m + 2, in which case Defect.)\n2. **My cooperation is pivotal or near-pivotal** (`m \u2212 2 \u2264 x \u2264 m`): Cooperate. My contribution likely makes or keeps the threshold satisfied.\n3. **Threshold badly missed** (`x < m \u2212 2`): Cooperate only if the recent trend is upward \u2014 i.e., `others_C[t\u22121] > others_C[t\u22122]` (treat missing t\u22122 as 0) \u2014 or if this is within the first \u2308r/4\u2309 rounds (keep trying to establish cooperation early). Otherwise Defect (don't waste contributions on a hopeless round).\n4. **Recovery rule:** If I defected last round and the threshold failed by exactly one cooperator, Cooperate this round regardless of other rules.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 no endgame defection. Specifically: Cooperate if `x \u2265 m \u2212 2` in round r\u22122; otherwise apply rule 3.\n\n**Persistent failure guard:** If the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation in all of them, Defect for one round, then resume Cooperate and repeat the cycle (probe for revival without permanently abandoning the group).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nx = others_C[t-1]\nif defected_last and threshold_missed_by_one: play C\nif x >= m+1:\n    play D with prob min(1, (x-m)/n) else C\nelif x >= m-2:\n    play C\nelse:\n    if t < ceil(r/4) or others_C[t-1] > others_C[t-2]: play C\n    else: play D\n# override: after 3 straight failures while cooperating,\n# play D once, then reset failure counter and resume C\n```\n\nThe default posture is cooperation: I cooperate whenever there is a realistic chance my contribution secures the reward for everyone, including the final round, and only withhold when the group has clearly abandoned the threshold or comfortably exceeds it without me."

description_PROSOCIAL_3 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at end of each round observe `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t. Track `success(t)` = whether threshold was met.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Decide based on last round:\n\n1. **Threshold succeeded last round:**\n   - If `coop_others(t\u22121) \u2265 m` (threshold would have been met even without me): Cooperate anyway *unless* `coop_others(t\u22121) \u2265 m + 1` (comfortable surplus of at least 2 beyond need), in which case Defect once to harvest the surplus, but return to Cooperate the following round regardless of outcome.\n   - If `coop_others(t\u22121) == m \u2212 1` (I was pivotal): Cooperate.\n   - If `coop_others(t\u22121) < m \u2212 1` but success occurred (impossible; ignore).\n\n2. **Threshold failed last round:**\n   - If `coop_others(t\u22121) \u2265 m \u2212 2` (we were close \u2014 my cooperation plus one more would fix it, or just mine): Cooperate, trying to lift the group over.\n   - If `coop_others(t\u22121) < m \u2212 2`: Cooperate with probability p = (coop_others(t\u22121) + 1) / m, otherwise Defect. This avoids wasting contributions in a hopeless group while continuing to signal willingness.\n\n3. **Persistent-failure cutoff:** If the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds AND `coop_others` averaged below m \u2212 2 over those rounds, Defect until a round occurs where `coop_others(t\u22121) \u2265 m \u2212 1`, then resume rule 1/2. (Re-probe with a single Cooperate every 3rd round of this dormant phase to test whether the group has recovered.)\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect merely because it's the final round. Exception: if in the dormant phase (rule 3 active), Defect.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    x = coop_others(t-1)\n    if dormant:\n        if x >= m-1: dormant = False; play C\n        elif t % 3 == 0: play C   # probe\n        else: play D\n    elif success(t-1):\n        if x >= m+1: play D        # harvest surplus one round\n        else: play C\n    else:  # failure\n        if x >= m-2: play C\n        else:\n            if last 3 rounds all failed and avg x < m-2: dormant = True; play D\n            else: play C with prob (x+1)/m else D\n    # after any harvest-defection (x >= m+1 case), force C next round\n```\n\nThe default disposition is cooperation: I contribute whenever my contribution is plausibly needed or the group is near the threshold, absorb the pivotal role willingly, only free-ride when there is clear excess cooperation, and only withdraw when the group has demonstrably abandoned the project \u2014 while still periodically probing to rebuild cooperation."

description_PROSOCIAL_4 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at the end of each round t, observe `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated. Let `need = m`.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Base decision on last round's observation.\n\nLet `x = coop_others(t-1)` (opponents only, 0 to n-1).\n\n1. **Success was comfortable without me needed:** if `x \u2265 m + 1` \u2192 the threshold would have been met even if one cooperator drops out; still **Cooperate** (prosocial default: don't free-ride on a healthy coalition \u2014 defecting invites cascade). Exception: if `x \u2265 m + 2` for two consecutive rounds, you may **Defect once** to bank surplus, then return to Cooperate the following round regardless of outcome (this \"probe\" is optional; skip it if m \u2265 n \u2212 1).\n\n2. **My cooperation is pivotal or nearly so:** if `m \u2212 2 \u2264 x \u2264 m` \u2192 **Cooperate.** The threshold hinges on players like me; contribute.\n\n3. **Hopeless environment:** if `x < m \u2212 2` \u2192 **Defect**, but with recovery attempts: cooperate anyway on \"olive-branch\" rounds, defined as every round where `t mod 3 == 0`, to signal willingness and re-seed cooperation. If an olive-branch round yields `x \u2265 m \u2212 2`, resume rule 2/1 behavior.\n\n**Streak tracking:** maintain `fail_streak` = consecutive rounds where the threshold was missed despite my cooperation. If `fail_streak \u2265 3`, switch to the hopeless-environment regime (rule 3) even if `x \u2265 m \u2212 2`. Reset `fail_streak` to 0 whenever the threshold is met.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do **not** defect merely because it's the final round. If the previous round met the threshold or `x \u2265 m \u2212 2`, Cooperate; otherwise Defect.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    x = coop_others(t-1)\n    if fail_streak >= 3:\n        play C if (t % 3 == 0) else D    # olive branch\n    elif x >= m - 2:\n        play C\n    else:\n        play C if (t % 3 == 0) else D\n\nupdate after round:\n    if threshold met: fail_streak = 0\n    elif I played C: fail_streak += 1\n```\n\nThe strategy opens cooperatively, keeps cooperating whenever success is plausible (including when it could free-ride), abandons doomed coalitions only after repeated failure, and periodically extends olive branches to rebuild cooperation."

description_PROSOCIAL_5 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Threshold Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `others_C[t]` = number of opponents who cooperated (0..n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `o = others_C[t\u22121]` (opponents' cooperators last round) and let `recent` = average of `others_C` over the last min(3, t) rounds.\n\n1. **Threshold nearly self-sustaining without me:** If `o \u2265 m + 1` (threshold met last round with at least 2 spare cooperators beyond need), defect this round \u2014 my contribution is redundant. But if this causes a failure (observed next round: threshold missed), immediately return to cooperating.\n2. **I am pivotal or near-pivotal:** If `o \u2208 {m\u22121, m}`, cooperate \u2014 my contribution likely makes or safely secures the threshold.\n3. **Hopeful shortfall:** If `m \u2212 ceil(n/3) \u2264 o < m \u2212 1`, cooperate with persistence: cooperate unless the group has failed the threshold in **3 consecutive rounds** while I cooperated, in which case defect for 1 round (signal/probe), then cooperate again.\n4. **Hopeless shortfall:** If `o < m \u2212 ceil(n/3)` AND `recent < m \u2212 1`, defect (contribution is wasted). Re-test cooperation every 3rd round (cooperate once) to check whether the group has recovered; if that probe round achieves \u2265 m\u22121 opponent-plus-me cooperators or opponent cooperation rises to \u2265 m\u22121, resume rule-based cooperation.\n\n**Failure recovery override:** Whenever the previous round failed (total cooperators < m) but `others_C[t\u22121] \u2265 m \u2212 2`, cooperate \u2014 the group was close and one more cooperator can tip it.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 no endgame defection. Cooperate if `o \u2265 m \u2212 ceil(n/3)` or the pivotal/near-pivotal conditions hold; defect only in the hopeless case or the redundancy case (rule 1).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\no = others_C[t-1]; recent = mean(others_C[max(0,t-3):t])\nif o >= m+1:\n    play D   # redundant; revert to C if threshold fails\nelif o >= m-1:\n    play C   # pivotal\nelif o >= m - ceil(n/3):\n    if failed_with_my_C_last_3_rounds: play D once, then C\n    else: play C\nelse:\n    if recent >= m-1: play C\n    elif t % 3 == 0: play C   # periodic probe\n    else: play D\n```\n\nDefault action in any ambiguous case: Cooperate."

description_PROSOCIAL_6 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at the end of each round t, observe `others_C(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated (out of n\u22121). Let `total_C(t)` = others_C(t) + my own contribution.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1 \u2014 decision rules, evaluated in order:**\n\n1. **Success momentum:** If the threshold was met last round (total_C(t\u22121) \u2265 m):\n   - If others_C(t\u22121) \u2265 m (threshold met even without me), play **D** with probability 0.5, else C \u2014 probe whether my contribution is pivotal without destabilizing the group. If this probe causes failure next round, return to C immediately and stop probing for the next 3 rounds.\n   - Otherwise (my cooperation was needed): play **C**.\n\n2. **Near miss:** If threshold failed but others_C(t\u22121) \u2265 m \u2212 2 (i.e., we were within 2 cooperators of success counting me): play **C** \u2014 keep pushing, success is within reach.\n\n3. **Hopeless round:** If others_C(t\u22121) < m \u2212 2: play **D** this round, but re-enter with **C** after one round of defection (i.e., alternate one D then one C) to signal willingness to rebuild. If others_C has been < m \u2212 2 for 3 consecutive rounds, switch to **D** permanently until others_C(t\u22121) \u2265 m \u2212 2 again, at which point resume rule 2.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 no endgame defection. Exception: if rule 3's permanent-D condition is active, play D.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif total_C(t-1) >= m:\n    if others_C(t-1) >= m and not recently_probed_badly:\n        play C with prob 0.5 else D\n    else: play C\nelif others_C(t-1) >= m - 2: play C\nelse:\n    if hopeless_streak >= 3: play D  (until others_C >= m-2)\n    else: alternate D, C\n```\n\nThe default posture is cooperation: I always cooperate when my contribution is plausibly pivotal, forgive single failures instantly, and only withhold contribution when the group is demonstrably far from the threshold \u2014 and even then I periodically cooperate to help restart collective success."

description_PROSOCIAL_7 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at the end of each round observe `coop_others` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated; total cooperators that round = `coop_others + c_me`.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1 \u2014 decision rule based on last round:**\n\nLet `L` = total cooperators last round.\n\n1. **Threshold met last round (L \u2265 m):**\n   - If L \u2265 m + 1 and I cooperated: there is slack \u2014 defect this round with probability only if slack is safe: defect if L \u2265 m + 2, else cooperate. (i.e., cooperate whenever L \u2208 {m, m+1}; if L \u2265 m+2, defect once to test, then return to this rule.)\n   - If I defected and L \u2265 m: cooperate this round (rejoin, don't free-ride repeatedly).\n\n2. **Threshold missed last round (L < m):**\n   - If L \u2265 m \u2212 2 (near miss): cooperate \u2014 the group is close; my contribution plausibly pivotal.\n   - If L < m \u2212 2 (far miss): enter a **probation check**: defect for one round, observing whether others rally. Then:\n     - If cooperation rose to \u2265 m \u2212 2 in that round, resume cooperating.\n     - Otherwise defect again, but every \u2308r/10\u2309 rounds (at least every 3 rounds) play one \"olive-branch\" cooperation to signal willingness to rebuild.\n\n3. **Hopeless-group cutoff:** Maintain a running count. If in the last 4 rounds the threshold was never met AND average total cooperators < m \u2212 2, defect except for the periodic olive-branch cooperations above.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect merely because it's the final round. Exception: if rule 3's hopeless condition holds, defect (no olive branch, since there's no future to signal for).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    L = cooperators last round\n    if hopeless():                      # rule 3\n        play C if olive_branch_due() and t < r-1 else D\n    elif L >= m + 2: play D             # exploit slack once\n    elif L >= m - 2: play C             # success or near-miss\n    else: play D once, then re-evaluate # probation check\n```\n\nTies and edge cases: after a slack-driven defection (L \u2265 m+2), always cooperate the following round regardless of outcome, ensuring I never defect twice consecutively while the group is succeeding. If m = n (everyone needed), never defect except under the hopeless condition, since any defection guarantees failure."

description_PROSOCIAL_8 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `coop_others[t]` = number of opponents who cooperated, and `success[t]` = whether the threshold was met.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Round t \u2265 1:** Let `x = coop_others[t-1]` (opponents' cooperators last round).\n\n1. **If x \u2265 m:** the threshold was met without needing me \u2014 Defect (my contribution is redundant), *unless* x == m exactly and success has failed in any of the last two rounds; in that fragile case, Cooperate as a safety buffer.\n2. **If x == m \u2212 1:** Cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal; my contribution turns failure into success (or maintained success last round).\n3. **If m \u2212 1 \u2212 d \u2264 x < m \u2212 1**, where `d = max(1, ceil((m-1)/3))`: Cooperate \u2014 the group is close to threshold; cooperate to signal and try to pull the group up.\n4. **If x < m \u2212 1 \u2212 d:** the group is far from threshold \u2014 Defect for this round to avoid wasted contributions, but **probe**: cooperate anyway with probability 0.25 to test whether the group can be revived. Additionally, always cooperate (full probe) if there have been two consecutive defect-rounds under this rule, then reset the probe counter.\n\n**Streak override:** If the threshold has been met in each of the last 3 rounds and my action last round was C, keep playing C (don't destabilize a working equilibrium), except when rule 1 clearly shows x > m.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect merely because the game ends. Specifically: cooperate if x from round r\u22122 is in [m \u2212 1 \u2212 d, m \u2212 1] or if the streak override applies; otherwise follow rules 1 and 4 as usual.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nx = coop_others[t-1]\nd = max(1, ceil((m-1)/3))\nif streak of 3 successes and I played C last round and x <= m: play C\nif x >= m:\n    if x == m and any failure in last 2 rounds: play C\n    else: play D\nelif x >= m - 1 - d: play C\nelse:\n    if two consecutive D-by-rule-4: play C (reset counter)\n    else: play C with prob 0.25, else D\n```"

description_ALTRUISTIC_1 = "**Altruistic Threshold-Guardian Strategy**\n\nCore principle: maximize the probability the group meets the threshold every round, sacrificing personal endowment whenever my contribution could plausibly matter.\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe `coop_others(t)` = number of other players who cooperated (out of n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = coop_others(t\u22121)`.\n\n1. If `x \u2265 m + 1` (threshold was met with at least 2 cooperators to spare besides me): Cooperate anyway \u2014 altruistic default, do not free-ride on surplus, since others may simultaneously drop out.\n   - Exception (surplus rotation for stability, optional): still cooperate. No defection here; the altruistic stance is to never gamble the threshold on others.\n\n2. If `m \u2212 (n\u22121) \u2264 x`, i.e., success is arithmetically possible: Cooperate. (My contribution may be pivotal.)\n\n3. Only defect if cooperation is provably futile over a sustained window: if in each of the last 3 rounds `coop_others < m \u2212 1` (threshold failed even counting my cooperation), then defect for 1 round as a probe-conservation step, then return to cooperation to attempt to re-seed the group. Formally:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse if last 3 rounds all had coop_others < m - 1: \n    play D this round, then resume C next round (reset window)\nelse: play C\n```\n\n4. **Recovery re-seeding:** After any futility-defection, unconditionally cooperate for the next 2 rounds regardless of history, signaling willingness to rebuild cooperation.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate, unless the futility condition in rule 3 holds (three consecutive hopeless rounds). No end-game defection: the altruistic strategy forgoes the tempting final-round free-ride to protect the group payoff of k for everyone.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n: always cooperate (I am always pivotal), never invoke futility defection.\n- If coop_others exactly equals m\u22121 last round (I was pivotal): cooperate \u2014 I am likely the keystone.\n- Ties/uncertainty always resolve toward C.\n\nIn short: cooperate essentially always; the only defections are single-round pauses after three consecutive rounds where the threshold failed by more than one cooperator, immediately followed by renewed cooperation attempts."

description_ALTRUISTIC_2 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Threshold Guardian**\n\nCore principle: maximize the chance the group meets the threshold every round, treating others' payoffs as valuable as my own. I cooperate whenever my cooperation could plausibly be needed, and defect only when it is provably useless or provably redundant \u2014 never to grab private gain at the group's expense.\n\nNotation: after each round I observe `coop_others(t)` = number of other players who cooperated in round t. Maintain `est` = a running estimate of others' cooperativeness, initialized optimistically.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. Signal willingness and help meet the threshold immediately.\n\n2. **Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = coop_others(t-1)` and update a smoothed estimate: `est \u2190 0.5\u00b7est + 0.5\u00b7x` (initialize `est = m` after round 0's observation, i.e., just use x for round 1).\n\n   - **If x \u2265 m + 1** (threshold met last round with at least 2 cooperators to spare, even without me): the group is safely over the threshold; cooperate anyway *unless* x \u2265 m + 2, in which case I may defect one round to test \u2014 but as an altruist, default rule: **still cooperate.** Redundant cooperation costs only me and adds robustness against simultaneous dropouts. So: cooperate.\n   \n   - **If m - n + 1 \u2264 x**, i.e., success was or is plausibly within reach: **cooperate.** This covers near-misses (x = m-1 or m-2): my contribution plus modest recovery by others can tip the threshold, so I always contribute.\n   \n   - **Hopeless-case exception:** Defect only if cooperation has been provably futile: if in each of the last 3 rounds `coop_others < m - 1` (even with my C the threshold failed) **and** `est < m - 2`, then defect for one round (conserve nothing at others' expense \u2014 success was impossible regardless). Resume cooperating immediately if `coop_others` in the defection round rises to \u2265 m - 2, or after 2 defection rounds regardless (periodic \"revival\" attempts to rebuild cooperation).\n\n3. **Last round (t = r - 1):** Cooperate, unless the hopeless-case exception is active. No end-game defection: an altruist does not exploit the final round, since defecting when the threshold is met at exactly m would destroy k for all n players to gain 1 for myself.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    x = coop_others(t-1)\n    hopeless = (last 3 rounds all had coop_others < m-1) and (est < m-2)\n    if hopeless and defect_streak < 2 and x < m-2:\n        play D; defect_streak += 1\n    else:\n        play C; defect_streak = 0\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- m = n (everyone needed): always cooperate; the hopeless exception still applies only after 3 consecutive total failures, then revival attempts continue every 2 rounds.\n- Noisy/oscillating opponents: the smoothed `est` prevents overreacting to a single bad round; a single failed round never triggers defection.\n- If the threshold succeeded in the previous round for any reason: cooperate unconditionally.\n\nThe strategy defects only when defection cannot harm anyone (threshold unreachable even with my contribution), and even then keeps probing to restart cooperation. It never free-rides on a met threshold."

description_ALTRUISTIC_3 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Threshold Guardian**\n\nCore principle: maximize the probability that the group reaches the threshold every round, treating my own endowment as expendable whenever it could plausibly help.\n\n**State tracked:**\n- coop_others[t]: number of other players who cooperated in round t\n- Estimate \u0109 = weighted average of coop_others over recent rounds (weight recent rounds more, e.g., exponential decay with factor 0.6; before round 0, \u0109 is undefined)\n\n**Decision rule for round t:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. (Signal willingness and immediately contribute toward m.)\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Cooperate unless my contribution is provably irrelevant in *both* directions:\n   - Let \u0109 = decayed average of coop_others.\n   - **Defect only if** \u0109 \u2265 m + 1.5 (threshold is safely met without me, with margin) \u2014 and even then, only if coop_others[t\u22121] \u2265 m + 2 in each of the last two rounds. Otherwise cooperate.\n   - If \u0109 \u2264 m \u2212 1 (group falling short), still **cooperate** \u2014 an altruist keeps contributing to pull others toward the threshold and never abandons the project, even after failures. The only exception: if coop_others has been 0 for **five consecutive rounds** (literally no one else ever cooperates and m \u2265 2, so success is impossible), cooperate anyway on every round t where t mod 3 == 0 (persistent beacon inviting coordination), defect otherwise. Resume full cooperation immediately if any opponent cooperates.\n\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same rule as above \u2014 no end-game defection. Cooperate unless the safe-surplus condition (\u0109 \u2265 m + 1.5 and last two rounds \u2265 m + 2 others) holds.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n (everyone needed): cooperate every round unconditionally, including the last.\n- If defecting under the surplus rule ever causes cooperators to drop below m + 1 in the next observed round, return to unconditional cooperation for the remainder of the game.\n- Ties/ambiguity: whenever any rule is borderline, choose C.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nif m == n: play C\n\u0109 = decayed_avg(coop_others)\nif \u0109 >= m + 1.5 and coop_others[t-1] >= m+2 and coop_others[t-2] >= m+2:\n    play D          # my token is redundant; let others keep the surplus habit\nelif last 5 rounds all had coop_others == 0 and m >= 2:\n    play C if t % 3 == 0 else D    # beacon mode\nelse:\n    play C\nif previously defected via surplus rule and coop_others dropped < m+1:\n    permanently disable surplus-defection; play C thereafter\n```"

description_ALTRUISTIC_4 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Threshold Guardian**\n\nCore principle: my goal is to maximize the number of rounds in which the threshold m is met, treating my own endowment as expendable.\n\nNotation: let `coop_others(t)` = number of other players who cooperated in round t; maintain history of these counts.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. Set an optimistic prior that others will cooperate.\n\n2. **Rounds t \u2265 1:** Estimate expected cooperators among others as a recency-weighted average:\n   - `est = 0.6 * coop_others(t-1) + 0.4 * (mean of coop_others over all previous rounds)`\n\n   Then:\n   - If `est \u2265 m` (threshold likely met even without me): **still cooperate**, unless `est \u2265 m + 2` (comfortable surplus of at least 2 beyond the threshold without me), in which case cooperating adds nothing to group success \u2014 but cooperate anyway if there is any recent volatility, defined as `max \u2212 min of coop_others over the last min(3, t) rounds \u2265 2`. Only defect when the surplus is \u2265 2 AND recent counts are stable.\n   - If `m \u2212 1 \u2264 est < m + 2`: **cooperate** \u2014 my contribution is plausibly pivotal.\n   - If `est < m \u2212 1` (group falling short even with me): **cooperate anyway** for up to 3 consecutive failed rounds, signaling willingness and giving conditional cooperators a foothold. After 3 consecutive rounds where total cooperators < m despite my cooperation, insert a single probe cycle: cooperate every round regardless (never abandon), i.e., in the hopeless regime simply **keep cooperating** \u2014 the altruistic stance accepts personal loss for any chance of collective recovery. (Exception: if `coop_others` has been 0 for 4 consecutive rounds, cooperate on even-indexed rounds and defect on odd ones as a low-cost beacon; resume full cooperation immediately when `coop_others \u2265 1`.)\n\n3. **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate unless `coop_others(r\u22122) = 0` and est < 1 (i.e., success is impossible even with me among a dead group). No end-game defection otherwise \u2014 even if est \u2265 m + 2, cooperate in the final round to guard against others' end-game defections.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play D if (coop_others(t-1) == 0 and est < 1) else C\nelse:\n    est = 0.6*coop_others(t-1) + 0.4*mean(history)\n    if est >= m+2 and stable_last3(): play D   # harmless free ride only when safe\n    elif zero_streak >= 4: play C if t even else D  # beacon mode\n    else: play C\n```\n\nCooperation is the default in every ambiguous situation; defection occurs only when it provably cannot harm collective success or when the group is verifiably dead."

description_ALTRUISTIC_5 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Threshold Guardian**\n\nCore principle: my payoff is secondary; maximize the chance the group reaches m cooperators every round, and only defect when my cooperation is provably irrelevant.\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Round t \u2265 1:** Let o = o_{t-1} (most recent observation) and \u014d = average of others' cooperation over all past rounds.\n\n1. **If o \u2265 m + 1 and \u014d \u2265 m + 1:** the threshold is comfortably met without me even with one dropout. Play D \u2014 but only for a single round, then re-cooperate next round regardless (probing rather than free-riding; the saved endowment is not the goal, avoiding wasted contributions is). If in doubt, cooperate.\n2. **Otherwise (o \u2264 m):** Cooperate. This includes:\n   - o = m \u2212 1 or o = m: my contribution is pivotal or near-pivotal \u2014 always C.\n   - o < m \u2212 1 (threshold failed even with me): still Cooperate. Persist as a beacon: a visible cooperator raises the count others see and may pull conditional cooperators toward the threshold. Never punish, never withhold in retaliation.\n\n3. **Hopeless-case exception:** If the threshold has failed in every round so far AND o_{t-1} \u2264 max(0, m \u2212 3) AND t \u2265 3 (others are far below the threshold and unresponsive), still Cooperate every round in which m \u2212 1 others could plausibly join (i.e., n \u2212 1 \u2265 m \u2212 1, always true). In short: no give-up clause \u2014 cooperate anyway. Altruism means absorbing the loss to keep success possible.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect for endgame gain. If rule 1 would fire, cooperate anyway (an extra cooperator costs the group nothing but insures against simultaneous endgame defections by others).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    o = others_cooperating[t-1]\n    avg = mean(others_cooperating[0..t-1])\n    if t < r-1 and o >= m+1 and avg >= m+1 and last_action == C:\n        play D        # single-round probe, redundant contribution\n    else:\n        play C\n```\n\nNet behavior: cooperate essentially always; defect only in interior rounds when at least m+1 others reliably cooperate (so success is guaranteed with a safety margin without me), and never two rounds in a row, never in the first or last round."

description_ALTRUISTIC_6 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Guardian (Threshold-Backstop Cooperator)**\n\nCore principle: my endowment is worth less to me than the group reward is to everyone; I sacrifice whenever there is any plausible chance my contribution helps or sustains the norm of cooperation.\n\nNotation: at round t, let coop(t\u22121) = number of *other* players who cooperated last round (observable), and let history give the sequence of these counts.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. Signal willingness immediately.\n\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (including the last round):** Cooperate, unless the \"hopeless\" condition below holds; then defect that round but remain ready to return.\n\n   **Hopeless condition:** defect in round t only if BOTH:\n   - coop(t\u22121) \u2264 m \u2212 2 (even with me, the threshold failed), AND\n   - the threshold has failed in the last min(3, t) consecutive rounds despite my cooperation in each of them.\n\n   In words: I keep contributing through failures for up to 3 rounds, absorbing losses to try to pull the group over the line. Only after three straight failures where my contribution was wasted do I pause for one round.\n\n3. **Probe after pausing:** After any defection, cooperate again the very next round (a one-round pause maximum). This gives the group repeated chances to reassemble.\n\n4. **Rescue override:** If coop(t\u22121) = m \u2212 1 or m \u2212 2 (the group is one or two cooperators short, or just at threshold counting me), always cooperate regardless of any failure streak \u2014 my single contribution is likely pivotal.\n\n5. **Never exploit:** Even if coop(t\u22121) \u2265 m (threshold met without me and I could free-ride), still cooperate. Altruism means I don't defect to skim extra payoff off others' contributions; my cooperation provides slack against others' random defections.\n\n6. **Last round:** No end-game defection. Apply the same rules; cooperate unless the hopeless condition holds.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    others = coop(t-1)\n    if others >= m - 2: play C            # pivotal or safe: always help\n    elif failed_streak_with_my_C >= 3 and last_action == C:\n        play D                             # single-round pause\n    else: play C\n```\n\nEdge cases: if m == n (all needed), I always cooperate except after 3 consecutive total failures, then pause one round and resume. If n is small or r \u2264 3, drop the pause rule entirely and cooperate every round."

description_ALTRUISTIC_7 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Guardian**\n\nCore principle: my payoff is secondary; maximize the chance the group reaches the threshold every round, sacrificing my endowment whenever it could plausibly help.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\nLet `coop_others(t-1)` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round.\n\n- **Round 0:** Cooperate.\n- **Round t \u2265 1:**\n  - If `coop_others(t-1) \u2265 m + 1`: there is comfortable slack even without me. Still **cooperate** \u2014 altruistic play never risks tipping the group below threshold to grab the private unit, and my cooperation buffers against others' defection drift. (Exception below.)\n  - If `coop_others(t-1) < m + 1`: **Cooperate** \u2014 my contribution is potentially pivotal.\n  - Only exception \u2014 hopelessness check: maintain a sliding window of the last w = min(3, t) rounds. If in *every* round of the window `coop_others < m \u2212 1` (i.e., even with my contribution the threshold failed and was never within one cooperator), then the group is unreachable; **defect** for one round, then resume cooperation (a one-round \"probe pause\") to re-test whether the environment has shifted. If the next observation again shows `coop_others < m \u2212 1`, alternate: cooperate one round, defect one round \u2014 this keeps periodically offering cooperation in case others coordinate, without permanently abandoning the group.\n  - The moment any round shows `coop_others \u2265 m \u2212 1`, exit hopelessness mode immediately and return to unconditional cooperation.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nstate: hopeless = False\n\ndef act(t, history):            # history = list of coop_others per past round\n    if t == 0: return C\n    last = history[-1]\n    if last >= m - 1:\n        hopeless = False\n        return C\n    window = history[-min(3, len(history)):]\n    if all(x < m - 1 for x in window):\n        hopeless = True\n    if hopeless:\n        # alternate: defect on even parity of rounds spent hopeless, cooperate on odd\n        return D if (rounds_in_hopeless % 2 == 0) else C\n    return C\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n\n- **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate under the same rules \u2014 no end-game defection. Altruism means forgoing the safe final-round free-ride even when the threshold looks secure.\n- **Exactly pivotal situations** (`coop_others == m \u2212 1` last round): always cooperate \u2014 never gamble with the group's outcome.\n- **Oversupply** (`coop_others \u2265 m` consistently): still cooperate; equal payoff for all cooperators is preferred to extracting private gains at others' risk.\n- **m = n:** cooperation is always pivotal; cooperate every round unconditionally except under the hopelessness alternation, which still offers C half the time.\n\nThe strategy defects only when repeated evidence shows my contribution is provably wasted (threshold unreachable even with me), and even then keeps extending cooperative offers indefinitely."

description_ALTRUISTIC_8 = "**Strategy: Unconditional Threshold Guardian**\n\nCore principle: maximize the probability the group reaches the threshold every round, treating my own endowment as expendable.\n\n**Decision rules:**\n\nLet `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Maintain an estimate of expected opponent cooperation:\n\n- `E = coop_others(t\u22121)` for the previous round, smoothed: `E_t = 0.5\u00b7E_{t\u22121} + 0.5\u00b7coop_others(t\u22121)`.\n\nEach round t:\n\n1. **Round 0:** Cooperate. (Signal willingness, help meet threshold immediately.)\n2. **Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (including the last round):**\n   - If `E_t \u2265 m` (opponents alone very likely to meet threshold) **and** `coop_others(t\u22121) \u2265 m + 1` (comfortable margin), defect this round \u2014 my contribution is redundant; but return to cooperation immediately if the margin shrinks (i.e., next round `coop_others < m+1`).\n   - Otherwise, **cooperate.**\n3. **Hopeless-case check:** Only if opponents have shown near-total defection for 3 consecutive rounds (`coop_others \u2264 m \u2212 3` each time, so even with my contribution the threshold badly fails), defect for one round as a probe, then cooperate again the following round to re-offer coordination. Repeat this probe cycle while hopelessness persists. If m \u2264 2, skip this rule entirely and always cooperate.\n4. **Last round:** Apply the same rules as any other round \u2014 no end-game defection. Cooperate unless my contribution is clearly redundant per rule 2.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    prev = coop_others(t-1)\n    E = 0.5*E + 0.5*prev\n    if prev >= m+1 and E >= m: play D      # redundant contribution\n    elif hopeless_streak >= 3 and m > 2 and not probed_last_round: play D  # single probe\n    else: play C\n```\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- After any round where the threshold failed and my cooperation would have made the difference (`coop_others == m \u2212 1`), cooperate for the next 3 rounds unconditionally, overriding all other rules.\n- If defecting under rule 2 and the threshold then fails, cooperate unconditionally for the rest of the game (my redundancy judgment proved wrong; err permanently on the side of contribution).\n- Ties/ambiguity always resolve to C."

description_BENEVOLENT_1 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at each round t > 0, let coop_prev = number of *other* players who cooperated last round (observed count, excluding me).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. Signal willingness and give the group its best chance to hit the threshold from the start.\n\n**Rounds t = 1 \u2026 r\u22121:** Cooperate unless the situation is clearly hopeless or my contribution is clearly wasted, judged as follows:\n\n1. **Threshold met without me last round** (coop_prev \u2265 m): the group is over-supplying. Cooperate anyway if coop_prev == m (my cooperation last round may have been part of that count under others' eyes \u2014 keep buffering with exactly-at-threshold safety). If coop_prev \u2265 m + 1, defect this round (the threshold is safely met without me); but return to cooperation immediately if the count ever drops to m or below.\n\n2. **Near miss** (m \u2212 2 \u2264 coop_prev \u2264 m): cooperate. My single contribution plausibly makes or preserves the threshold \u2014 this is where benevolent effort matters most.\n\n3. **Far from threshold** (coop_prev < m \u2212 2): the group failed badly. Still cooperate for a grace period: keep cooperating as long as the round-over-round trend in coop_prev is non-decreasing, or for the first \u2308r/4\u2309 rounds regardless. If coop_prev < m \u2212 2 for two consecutive rounds with a non-increasing trend after the grace period, defect (contribution is wasted), but **probe** by cooperating again every 3rd round to test whether the group has recovered; if a probe round shows coop_prev \u2265 m \u2212 2, resume rule 2 behavior.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** No end-game defection. Apply the same rules as above \u2014 cooperate whenever coop_prev in round r\u22122 was in [m\u22122, m]. Benevolence means not exploiting the final round: if success is plausible, contribute.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    x = others_cooperating(t-1)\n    if x >= m + 1: play D          # threshold safe without me\n    elif x >= m - 2: play C        # pivotal zone\n    else:                          # deep failure\n        if t < ceil(r/4): play C   # grace period\n        elif trend_nondecreasing(x): play C\n        elif t % 3 == 0: play C    # periodic probe\n        else: play D\n```\n\n**Benevolent alignment:** default to cooperation; only withhold when contribution is either redundant (comfortably above threshold) or demonstrably futile (persistent deep failure), and even then keep probing to help restart collective success. Never defect strategically to free-ride on an exactly-met threshold, and never exploit the final round."

description_BENEVOLENT_2 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = coop_others(t-1)` (opponents who cooperated last round).\n\n1. **Threshold met last round with me needed or comfortably:**\n   - If `x \u2265 m`: the group succeeded even without me. Still cooperate if `x < m + 1` is borderline? Rule: cooperate iff `x \u2264 m + 1` (keep supporting a near-threshold coalition); defect only if `x \u2265 m + 2` (large surplus \u2014 my contribution is redundant), but return to cooperation immediately if the count drops below `m + 2` afterwards.\n2. **Threshold met exactly because of me:** If `x = m - 1` (success required my C, or would have): cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal.\n3. **Near miss:** If `m - 3 \u2264 x \u2264 m - 2` (threshold missed by one or two): cooperate, signaling willingness to tip the group over.\n4. **Hopeless round:** If `x < m - 3`: defect this round, but \"probe\" by cooperating again every 3rd such round (i.e., cooperate if the number of consecutive hopeless rounds so far is a multiple of 3) to test whether the group can be revived.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelse:\n    x = opponents_cooperating(t-1)\n    if x >= m + 2: play D          # redundant surplus\n    elif x >= m - 3: play C        # pivotal or near-threshold: support\n    else:                          # hopeless\n        if consecutive_hopeless % 3 == 0: play C   # probe\n        else: play D\n```\n\n**Last round (t = r - 1):** Apply the same rule \u2014 no end-game defection. If the previous round had `x \u2265 m - 3`, cooperate; benevolence means not exploiting the final round.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If `m = n`: always cooperate unless the group has failed 3+ consecutive rounds with `x < m - 3`, then follow the probe cycle.\n- If my defection last round caused a failure (`x = m - 1` and I played D): cooperate unconditionally this round as repair.\n- Ties in counting include only opponents; my own action is added when reasoning about pivotality.\n\n**Benevolent alignment:** The strategy always cooperates when it could plausibly be pivotal, never free-rides on exact-threshold coalitions, sacrifices payoff in the last round to preserve group success, forgives failures quickly (one near-miss round suffices to restore cooperation), and periodically probes even hopeless groups rather than abandoning them permanently. Defection occurs only when contribution is clearly redundant (`x \u2265 m + 2`) or the group is far from viable \u2014 minimizing waste without ever undermining a functioning collective."

description_BENEVOLENT_3 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nLet `coop[t]` = total cooperators observed in round t (opponents' count + my own action).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121:** Let `others = coop[t\u22121] \u2212 c_me[t\u22121]` (opponents who cooperated last round).\n\n1. **If others \u2265 m:** The threshold is safely met without me. Cooperate anyway if others = m (my past contribution may have been pivotal in others' eyes \u2014 keep the buffer stable); if others \u2265 m + 1, defect this round (harmless free ride), but return to cooperation immediately if `coop` drops below m + 1 in the next observation.\n\n   Pseudocode:\n   - if others \u2265 m + 1: play D\n   - if others = m: play C\n\n2. **If m \u2212 1 \u2264 others \u2264 m:** My cooperation is likely pivotal. Cooperate.\n\n3. **If others < m \u2212 1:** The threshold failed and I alone can't fix it. Still cooperate, but with patience limits:\n   - Track `fail_streak` = consecutive rounds with coop[t] < m.\n   - Cooperate while `fail_streak \u2264 2` (signal willingness, invite recovery).\n   - If `fail_streak \u2265 3`: defect, but **probe**: cooperate once every 3rd round of continued failure to test whether the group can recover. If any probe or observation shows others \u2265 m \u2212 1, reset `fail_streak = 0` and resume rule 2's cooperation.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules as above \u2014 no end-game defection. If others \u2265 m \u2212 1 was observed in round r\u22122, cooperate; only defect if in the probe-off phase (fail_streak \u2265 3 and not a probe round) or if others \u2265 m + 1.\n\n**Tie-breaking / defaults:** Whenever uncertain (rules conflict or history is ambiguous), play C.\n\n**Summary of intent:** Always cooperate when pivotal or near-pivotal, absorb occasional exploitation, only withhold contribution when it's demonstrably wasted (persistent group failure) or clearly superfluous (comfortable surplus), and continually probe to restore collective success."

description_BENEVOLENT_4 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at end of each round observe `others_C(t)` = number of opponents (of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Track `coops_needed = m`.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = others_C(t\u22121)` (opponents' cooperation last round).\n\n1. **If x \u2265 m:** the threshold was met without needing me. Cooperate anyway (my contribution costs me only 1 vs. keeping the group safely above threshold; benevolently pad the margin) \u2014 *except* if `x \u2265 m + 1` for two consecutive rounds, in which case defect this round to conserve endowment, then resume cooperating (never defect two rounds in a row under this clause).\n2. **If m \u2212 1 \u2264 x < m** (i.e., x = m \u2212 1): my cooperation is pivotal. Cooperate.\n3. **If m \u2212 2 \u2265 x \u2265 ceil(m/2):** threshold narrowly missed. Cooperate \u2014 signal willingness and try to pull the group up.\n4. **If x < ceil(m/2):** cooperation is collapsing. Enter \"probe\" mode: defect, but cooperate every third round (rounds where `t mod 3 == 0`) as a low-cost olive branch. Exit probe mode (return to rules 1\u20133) as soon as any round shows `x \u2265 ceil(m/2)`.\n\n**Recovery override:** If the threshold was met in the previous round (total cooperators including me \u2265 m), always cooperate this round regardless of other rules \u2014 never be the one to break a working equilibrium.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Apply the same rules \u2014 cooperate whenever x from the previous round was \u2265 ceil(m/2)\u22121 or the threshold was met. Do not defect purely because it's the final round; if my cooperation may be pivotal (x in {m\u22121, m\u22122}), cooperate.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n (everyone needed): cooperate every round unless the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation; then apply probe mode.\n- Ties/uncertainty: whenever rules conflict, cooperate.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif threshold_met(t-1): play C   # recovery override\nelse:\n    x = others_C(t-1)\n    if x >= m: play C unless (x >= m+1 twice in a row and I cooperated last round) \u2192 D\n    elif x >= ceil(m/2): play C\n    else:  # probe mode\n        play C if t % 3 == 0 else D\n```\n\nThe default disposition is cooperation: I contribute whenever there is a realistic chance the group reaches the threshold, sacrifice my endowment when pivotal, never punish, and periodically extend cooperation even after collective failure to invite recovery."

description_BENEVOLENT_5 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator**\n\nMaintain after each round t: coop_others(t) = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let x = coop_others(t\u22121).\n\n1. If x \u2265 m: the group succeeded without needing me (there were at least m cooperators among the others). Defect this round \u2014 my contribution is likely redundant. But if this defection causes failure (observed x < m next round while x_prev \u2265 m came only barely, i.e., total cooperators last round was exactly m including opponents), return to cooperation immediately. Concretely: defect only if x \u2265 m; otherwise proceed below.\n\n2. If x = m\u22121: cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal; my contribution turns failure into success (or maintained success last round if I cooperated).\n\n3. If m\u22121 > x \u2265 m\u22121\u2212\u2308(m\u22121)/3\u2309 (near miss): cooperate, attempting to rally the threshold. Track consecutive failed near-miss attempts; if I have cooperated in \u2308r/4\u2309 consecutive rounds without the threshold ever being met, defect for one round (signal/probe), then resume cooperation if x rises.\n\n4. If x < m\u22121\u2212\u2308(m\u22121)/3\u2309 (hopeless): defect this round, but \"probe\" by cooperating once every 3 rounds to test whether the group has recovered.\n\n**Hysteresis on rule 1:** If I defected because x \u2265 m and the threshold then failed (total cooperators < m), cooperate for the next 2 rounds unconditionally to restore success, then resume normal rules.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 cooperate if last round's x was in {m\u22121} or the near-miss band. Do not defect for endgame reasons; only defect if x \u2265 m (redundant) or hopeless.\n\n**Benevolent orientation:** Default toward cooperation whenever my contribution plausibly matters (pivotal or near-miss cases, first round, recovery after a slip), never punish, and forgive immediately: any single round where the threshold is met resets all failure counters to zero. Defection occurs only when cooperation is provably redundant (x \u2265 m) or demonstrably futile (deep shortfall with periodic probing to give the group repeated chances to recover)."

description_BENEVOLENT_6 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivotal Cooperator**\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (0 \u2264 o_t \u2264 n\u22121). Maintain no per-player tracking (anonymous).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate.\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let o = o_{t\u22121} (others' cooperation last round).\n\n1. If o \u2265 m: Cooperate. (Group is safely above threshold; keep momentum \u2014 do not free-ride even though defection would likely still succeed. Benevolence: never exploit a working coalition.)\n2. If o = m\u22121 or o = m\u22122: Cooperate. (My contribution is pivotal or near-pivotal; without me the threshold likely fails.)\n3. If o \u2264 m\u22123: enter **testing mode** \u2014 Defect, except cooperate on \"probe\" rounds. Probe schedule: cooperate whenever (t mod 3 == 0), or immediately after any round where o increased by at least 2 relative to the previous round (signals reviving cooperation). If a probe round achieves o \u2265 m\u22122, exit testing mode and return to rules 1\u20132 next round.\n\n**Grace override:** If the threshold was actually met last round (total cooperators including me \u2265 m), always cooperate this round regardless of the rules above.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules \u2014 do not defect just because it's the final round. If the threshold was met in round r\u22122, cooperate; if in testing mode with o \u2264 m\u22123, defect (contribution would be wasted).\n\n**Tie-with-forgiveness:** If the group has failed the threshold for 3 consecutive rounds while I cooperated every time, switch to testing mode even if o = m\u22121 or m\u22122 (avoid being a perpetual sucker in a doomed group), but continue probing every 3rd round to offer a restart.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif threshold_met(t-1): play C\nelse:\n    o = others_cooperating(t-1)\n    if o >= m - 2:\n        if consecutive_failures_while_I_cooperated >= 3 and probe_not_due(t): play D\n        else: play C\n    else:\n        if t % 3 == 0 or o - others_cooperating(t-2) >= 2: play C   # probe\n        else: play D\n```\n\nThe default posture is cooperation: I contribute whenever there is a realistic chance the threshold is reached, sacrifice private payoff to be pivotal, never free-ride on a successful coalition, and repeatedly extend probes to rebuild cooperation after collapse \u2014 withholding only when contribution is demonstrably futile."

description_BENEVOLENT_7 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivotal Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at end of each round observe `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. (Signal willingness; threshold success is worth more than the saved endowment since k > 1.)\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Let `x = coop_others(t-1)`.\n\n- If `x \u2265 m`: the group succeeded without needing me last round. Cooperate anyway if my cooperation last round was pivotal-adjacent \u2014 specifically, cooperate if `x \u2264 m + 1` (stay in the coalition as a safety buffer); defect only if `x \u2265 m + 2` (ample slack; my defection cannot endanger the threshold).\n- If `x = m - 1` or `x = m`: cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal or near-pivotal; my contribution likely decides success.\n- If `m - 3 \u2264 x < m - 1`: cooperate \u2014 the group is close; keep pulling toward the threshold rather than triggering collapse.\n- If `x < m - 3`: enter a probing pattern \u2014 cooperate with probability 0.5 (or deterministically: cooperate on even rounds, defect on odd rounds). This avoids being endlessly exploited by a hopeless group while continuously offering a path back to cooperation.\n\n**Recovery override:** If in the probing state and `coop_others` rises to `\u2265 m - 2` in any round, immediately return to full cooperation next round.\n\n**Streak tolerance:** Never defect two rounds in a row unless `coop_others < m - 3` held in both of the last two rounds. This keeps me a reliable coalition member despite noise.\n\n**Last round (t = r - 1):** No special defection. Apply the same rules as above: cooperate whenever `coop_others(r-2) \u2265 m - 3`. Since k > 1, cooperating when it plausibly sustains the threshold beats keeping the endowment; I do not end-game defect on a working coalition.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nx = coop_others(t-1)\nif x >= m + 2:              play D\nelif x >= m - 3:            play C\nelse:                       # probing\n    if x_recovered_to >= m-2 recently: play C\n    else: play C if t is even else D\n```\n\n**Benevolence:** The strategy starts cooperatively, cooperates whenever there is any realistic chance of reaching the threshold, forgives instantly, never punishes, never exploits the final round, and defects only when the threshold is either safely met without it or clearly out of reach."

description_BENEVOLENT_8 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Cooperator (\"Pull Your Weight\")**\n\nNotation: after each round t, let coop(t) = total cooperators that round (including me), and others(t) = coop(t) \u2212 c_me.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate. (Signal willingness; threshold success benefits everyone.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Cooperate unless the group has shown itself hopeless or my contribution is clearly redundant. Specifically:\n\n1. Compute expected other-cooperators: est = others(t\u22121), smoothed as est = 0.7\u00b7others(t\u22121) + 0.3\u00b7others(t\u22122) when available (round the result).\n2. Decision:\n   - If est \u2265 m: cooperate anyway if est == m (my cooperation buffers against dropout); defect only if est \u2265 m + 1 (threshold safely met without me \u2014 free capacity, no harm done).\n   - If est == m \u2212 1 or est == m \u2212 2: cooperate \u2014 I am potentially pivotal or near-pivotal.\n   - If est < m \u2212 2: cooperate only if there is recent evidence of recovery (others(t\u22121) > others(t\u22122)); otherwise defect this round, but **probe** by cooperating once every 3 rounds to test whether the group can be revived.\n3. Forgiveness override: after any round where the threshold was met, cooperate in the next round regardless of the rules above (reinforce success).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same rules as above \u2014 do not switch to end-game defection. If est \u2208 {m\u22122, ..., m}, cooperate (pivotality matters most now); if est \u2265 m+1, defect; if est < m\u22122, defect (no future to invest in via probing).\n\n**Benevolence:** The default is cooperation; defection occurs only when it costs the group nothing (surplus cooperators) or when the group has repeatedly failed and my contribution is wasted \u2014 and even then I periodically probe to restart cooperation. I never punish, never exploit successful rounds by defecting into a bare-minimum coalition (I stay in when est == m), and I forgive immediately after any success."

description_SELFISH_1 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Contributor with Endgame Defection**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal to reaching the threshold; free-ride whenever the group appears to succeed (or hopelessly fail) without me.\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Maintain an estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of opponent cooperation, \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_{t\u22121} + 0.4\u00b7\u00f4 (initialized below).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil((n+1)/2) and k \u2265 1.5; otherwise defect. (Cheap thresholds are worth seeding; hard ones aren't worth solo risk.) Initialize \u00f4 = (n\u22121)\u00b7(m/n).\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Based on last round's opponent count o = o_{t\u22121}:\n\n1. If o \u2265 m: defect \u2014 threshold met without me last round; free-ride and pocket 1 + k.\n2. If o = m\u22121 or o = m\u22122: cooperate \u2014 I am (near-)pivotal; paying 1 to secure k > 1 is profitable, and a one-cooperator buffer guards against a single dropout.\n3. If o \u2264 m\u22123: defect \u2014 the cause is likely lost; don't waste the endowment. Exception: if \u00f4 \u2265 m\u22122 (recent trend suggests recovery) and k \u2265 2, cooperate once as a probe; if the threshold still fails, revert to defection until o rises to \u2265 m\u22122 again.\n\nAnti-exploitation check: if I have cooperated in the last 3 rounds and the threshold failed in all 3, defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of the rules above (stop subsidizing a losing group).\n\nAnti-freeride-collapse check: if rule 1 fired last round (I defected after o \u2265 m) and the threshold then failed with o = m\u22121 (my defection broke it), cooperate this round \u2014 I was actually pivotal.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate only if I am strictly pivotal by best estimate: cooperate iff o_{r\u22122} \u2208 {m\u22121, m\u22122} and k > 1. Otherwise defect \u2014 no future to invest in, so only pay when payment plausibly buys the reward this round.\n\n**Edge parameters:**\n- If m = n: cooperate every round except abandon permanently after any round where o < n\u22121 (one defector makes success impossible; never pay again).\n- If k is very large (k \u2265 3): loosen rule 3 to cooperate at o = m\u22123 as well during rounds t < r/2.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if (m <= ceil((n+1)/2) and k >= 1.5) else D\nif m == n: return C if all previous rounds had o == n-1 else D\nif last3_coops_all_failed: return D\nif t == r-1: return C if o in {m-1, m-2} and k > 1 else D\nif o >= m:\n    return D\nelif o >= m-2:\n    return C\nelif o == m-3 and k >= 3 and t < r/2:\n    return C\nelif \u00f4 >= m-2 and k >= 2 and not recently_probed:\n    return C  # probe\nelse:\n    return D\n```"

description_SELFISH_2 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivotality with Endgame Defection**\n\nNotation: at round t > 0, let o_{t-1} = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round, and let my last action be a_{t-1}.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1 \u2014 i.e., cooperate when the threshold looks plausibly reachable; otherwise defect. (If m > about half the players, initial success is unlikely and cooperation would be wasted.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (main phase):** Estimate expected opponent cooperators using an exponential average:\n```\nE_t = 0.6 * o_{t-1} + 0.4 * E_{t-1}   (E_0 = o_0)\n```\nDecide by pivotality:\n1. If E_t \u2265 m + 0.5 (rounded expectation \u2265 m even without me): **Defect** \u2014 free-ride, threshold met anyway.\n2. If m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 E_t < m + 0.5 (my contribution is likely pivotal): **Cooperate** \u2014 paying 1 to secure k > 1 is profitable.\n3. If E_t < m \u2212 1.5 (threshold unreachable even with me): **Defect** \u2014 don't waste the endowment.\n\nOverride for free-rider punishment resistance: if I defected last round and the threshold *failed* by exactly one cooperator (total cooperators = m\u22121), cooperate this round regardless \u2014 my defection was the cause and switching restores the surplus.\n\nOverride for exploitation check: track how often I cooperate while others coast. If in the last 3 rounds I cooperated each time and total cooperators exceeded m by \u2265 2 each time (I was non-pivotal), defect once to test whether the threshold survives without me; resume rules above afterward.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same pivotality rules, but tighten condition 2: cooperate only if E_t is in [m\u22121, m) exactly \u2014 i.e., only if the threshold appears to fail *by exactly the margin I can cover*. Otherwise defect, since there is no future to protect and k > 1 still makes a genuinely pivotal contribution profitable, but nothing else does.\n\n**Persistent-failure cutoff:** If the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation in all of them, defect for the remainder of the game unless a later round shows o_{t-1} \u2265 m\u22121, in which case re-enter the main-phase rules."

description_SELFISH_3 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Conditional Cooperator\"**\n\nNotation: each round observe o_t = number of *other* cooperators last round (out of n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1 (threshold plausibly reachable without me carrying it alone); otherwise cooperate anyway if k \u2265 2 (large prize justifies probing), else defect.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Base decision on o_{t\u22121}:\n\n- If o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m: threshold met without my help \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride; my contribution is not pivotal).\n- If o_{t\u22121} = m\u22121: I am pivotal \u2192 **Cooperate** (paying 1 to gain k > 1 is strictly profitable).\n- If o_{t\u22121} = m\u22122: **Cooperate** with encouragement \u2014 cooperate if k \u2265 1.5, else cooperate only if the group met the threshold in at least half of the past rounds.\n- If o_{t\u22121} \u2264 m\u22123: **Defect** (group too far from threshold; contribution likely wasted). Exception: every 3rd consecutive failing round, cooperate once as a probe *only if* k \u2265 2 and the deficit is exactly m\u22123, to test whether others are also conditional cooperators.\n\n**Anti-exploitation guard:** Track W = number of past rounds where I cooperated and threshold still failed. If W \u2265 3 and success rate of my cooperative rounds < 1/3, switch to permanent **Defect** except when o_{t\u22121} = m\u22121 (always take a sure pivotal gain).\n\n**Oscillation damping:** If the last two rounds alternated between (o \u2265 m) and (o = m\u22121) \u2014 indicating other conditional cooperators cycling with me \u2014 cooperate when o_{t\u22121} = m\u22121 *and also* when o_{t\u22121} = m, once per two rounds, to stabilize the threshold at exactly m and keep the k-flow coming.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** No future to influence, so act purely on immediate expected value: cooperate only if o_{t\u22121} = m\u22121 (pivotal, guaranteed net gain of k\u22121 if behavior persists) or if o_{t\u22121} = m\u22122 and k \u2265 3. Otherwise defect and pocket the endowment.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: C if (m <= ceil(n/2)+1 or k >= 2) else D\nelif t == r-1:\n    C if o == m-1 or (o == m-2 and k >= 3) else D\nelif guard_triggered:\n    C if o == m-1 else D\nelse:\n    if o >= m: D  (unless oscillation-damping turn \u2192 C)\n    elif o == m-1: C\n    elif o == m-2: C if (k >= 1.5 or hist_success >= 0.5) else D\n    else: D (with rare probe if k >= 2 and o == m-3)\n```\n\nThe core selfish logic: contribute only when the contribution is likely pivotal to unlocking k for myself; free-ride whenever the threshold clears without me; abandon hopeless groups quickly; never sacrifice the final-round endowment without a near-certain pivotal payoff."

description_SELFISH_4 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: let `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t; my action in round t is a_t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1; otherwise defect. (Cooperate when the threshold is plausibly reachable; if m is near n, first-round success is unlikely and contributing is wasted.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Estimate opponent cooperation from the previous round. Let x = coop_others(t\u22121). Decide based on pivotality:\n\n- If x \u2265 m: threshold met without me last round \u2192 **Defect** (free ride).\n- If x = m \u2212 1: I am likely pivotal \u2192 **Cooperate** (my contribution converts payoff from 1 to k, and k > 1, so being pivotal is strictly profitable).\n- If x = m \u2212 2: **Cooperate** once as a probe (opponents may match rising cooperation), but only if my last probe wasn't wasted: cooperate iff I did not cooperate in round t\u22121 while the threshold failed. Otherwise defect.\n- If x \u2264 m \u2212 3: threshold hopeless \u2192 **Defect** and keep my endowment.\n\nAdditional smoothing: maintain a running exponential average x\u0304 \u2190 0.5\u00b7x\u0304 + 0.5\u00b7x (initialized to x of round 0) and use round(x\u0304) instead of raw x when the raw x fluctuates (i.e., when |x \u2212 previous x| \u2265 2). This avoids being exploited by noisy or alternating opponents.\n\n**Exploitation guard:** track wasted contributions w = number of rounds where I cooperated and the threshold still failed. If w \u2265 3 consecutive such rounds, defect for the remainder unless x \u2265 m \u2212 1 in the immediately preceding round (i.e., only cooperate again when pivotality is near-certain).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate iff coop_others(r\u22122) is exactly m \u2212 1 (only when pivotal, since being pivotal yields k > 1 vs 1). Otherwise defect \u2014 no future to invest in, so never probe or build reputation.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if (m <= ceil(n/2)+1) else D\nx = coop_others(t-1)\nif t == r-1: return C if x == m-1 else D\nif guard_active and x < m-1: return D\nif x >= m: return D\nif x == m-1: return C\nif x == m-2 and not (my_last == C and threshold_failed_last): return C\nreturn D\n```"

description_SELFISH_5 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Contributor\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal to reaching the threshold; free-ride whenever the group seems able (or hopelessly unable) to meet it without me.\n\nNotation: let `o_t` = number of cooperating opponents observed in round t (out of n\u22121). Maintain an estimate `E` of expected opponent cooperators for the next round:\n\n- E \u2190 o_0 after round 0; thereafter E \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_t + 0.4\u00b7E (recency-weighted average).\n\n**Round 0:**\n- Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil((n+1)/2) and k \u2265 1.5; otherwise defect. (Seed cooperation only when the threshold is modest and the reward comfortably exceeds the contribution cost; else probe by defecting.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (decision rule each round):**\n1. If E \u2265 m + 0.5: **Defect** \u2014 threshold likely met without me; free-ride.\n2. Else if E \u2265 m \u2212 1.5 (i.e., roughly m\u22121 or m\u22120.5 opponents expected): **Cooperate** \u2014 I am likely pivotal, and gaining k > 1 beats keeping 1.\n3. Else (E < m \u2212 1.5): **Defect** \u2014 threshold unreachable even with me; contribution would be wasted. Exception: if E \u2265 m \u2212 2 and k \u2265 3, cooperate with probability 0.5 to attempt to restart coordination (cheap gamble given the large prize).\n\nFailure adjustment: if the threshold was missed by exactly 1 in the previous round and I defected, cooperate this round regardless of E (I was the missing piece; test whether stepping in fixes it).\n\nExploitation guard: track `wasted` = number of rounds where I cooperated and the threshold still failed. If wasted \u2265 3 consecutively, defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of rules above, then reset the counter.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):**\nSame pivotal logic \u2014 no reputation left to protect, so pure marginal calculus:\n- Cooperate iff m \u2212 2 < E < m + 0.5 and k > 1 (my contribution plausibly swings the outcome, and k > 1 makes swinging it profitable).\n- Otherwise defect and pocket the endowment.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n: I am always pivotal when everyone else cooperates; cooperate whenever o_{t\u22121} = n\u22121, defect after any observed defection (threshold is dead).\n- If E fluctuates wildly (variance of last 3 observations > 1.5), bias toward defection by requiring E \u2265 m \u2212 1 (instead of m \u2212 1.5) to cooperate \u2014 don't pay for unreliable partners."

description_SELFISH_6 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivot Cooperator**\n\nNotation: let t be the current round (0-indexed), o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observed after each round), and coop_t = total cooperators including me.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1 (threshold plausibly reachable without me being exploited); otherwise cooperate anyway only if k \u2265 2 (big prize justifies probing). Else defect.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Base the decision on last round's observation of others, o_{t\u22121}:\n\n1. **Surplus (o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m + 1):** Defect \u2014 threshold met without me; free-ride.\n2. **Exactly enough without me (o_{t\u22121} = m):** Defect, but if this defection causes failure next round (i.e., others drop below m after I drop out), return to rule 3 logic the following round.\n3. **Pivotal zone (o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 1):** Cooperate \u2014 my contribution likely tips the threshold, and k > 1 means the reward exceeds my kept endowment.\n4. **Near miss (o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 2):** Cooperate only if the recent trend is upward (o_{t\u22121} > o_{t\u22122}) or if k \u2265 2 (large upside justifies pulling others up). Otherwise defect.\n5. **Hopeless (o_{t\u22121} \u2264 m \u2212 3):** Defect \u2014 don't waste endowment on a failing project.\n\n**Streak override (give-up rule):** If the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation, defect until o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m \u2212 1 reappears; the group is not responsive and cooperation is pure loss.\n\n**Oscillation damping:** If my rule-2 defection caused failure last round (o dropped from m to below m), and o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 1 or m \u2212 2, cooperate for one round to restore the equilibrium, then resume normal rules. Track a flag `just_free_rode` to detect this.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate only if o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 1 exactly (strictly pivotal expectation: paying 1 to gain k > 1 is profitable even one-shot). In all other cases defect \u2014 no future to invest in.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C if (m <= ceil(n/2)+1) or k >= 2 else D\nelif t == r-1: play C iff o_{t-1} == m-1\nelse:\n    if fail_streak >= 3 and o_{t-1} < m-1: play D\n    elif o_{t-1} >= m+1: play D\n    elif o_{t-1} == m: play D  # free-ride\n    elif o_{t-1} == m-1: play C\n    elif o_{t-1} == m-2: play C if (k >= 2 or o_{t-1} > o_{t-2}) else D\n    else: play D\nupdate fail_streak: +1 if I played C and threshold failed, reset to 0 otherwise\n```\n\nThe core selfish logic: cooperate only when my single contribution is plausibly pivotal (net gain k \u2212 1 > 0), free-ride whenever the threshold is safe without me, and abandon ship entirely when the group can't reach the threshold \u2014 never pay for a lost cause or an already-won one."

description_SELFISH_7 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Contributor with Endgame Defection\"**\n\nNotation: at each round t, let o_t = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t\u22121. Maintain a running estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of recent opponent cooperation: after each round, \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_t + 0.4\u00b7\u00f4. Track `success_streak` = consecutive rounds threshold was met, and `fail_streak` likewise.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil((n+1)/2) (threshold plausibly reachable and my contribution likely pivotal); otherwise defect. Exception: if m = 1... (not possible, m > 1). If k is large relative to 1 (k \u2265 2), lean cooperative even for m up to ceil(0.6\u00b7n): cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(0.6\u00b7n) when k \u2265 2, else the majority rule above.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (main phase):** Decide based on predicted opponent cooperation \u00f4:\n\n1. **Free-ride check:** If \u00f4 \u2265 m + 0.5 (threshold likely met without me), play D.\n2. **Pivotal check:** If m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 \u00f4 < m + 0.5 (my cooperation plausibly decisive), play C \u2014 the reward k > 1 exceeds the endowment 1, so being pivotal pays.\n3. **Lost cause check:** If \u00f4 < m \u2212 1.5 (threshold likely fails even with me), play D \u2014 don't waste the endowment. Exception (probe): if fail_streak \u2264 2 and last round's cooperators (including me) were within 2 of m, play C once more to try to tip coordination; after 3 consecutive failures, defect until o_t \u2265 m \u2212 1 reappears.\n4. **Streak exploitation:** If I've cooperated and the threshold was met with strictly more than m cooperators total in the last round, defect this round (test if I'm dispensable). If that defection causes failure (total cooperators fell below m), return to cooperating next round.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Defect unless strictly pivotal: play C only if \u00f4 is in [m\u22121.25, m\u22120.5] \u2014 i.e., the threshold almost certainly fails without me and likely succeeds with me, making C's expected gain (\u2248k) exceed the kept endowment (1). Otherwise D \u2014 no future rounds means no reputational reason to contribute when not pivotal.\n\n**Second-to-last round (t = r\u22122):** Apply main-phase rules but raise the free-ride bar: defect if \u00f4 \u2265 m (anticipating others' endgame defection makes success less likely; don't waste contributions on doomed rounds). If \u00f4 is well above m (\u00f4 \u2265 m+1), still defect and pocket the endowment.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: C iff m <= ceil(0.6*n) if k>=2 else m <= ceil((n+1)/2)\nelif t == r-1: C iff m-1.25 <= \u00f4 <= m-0.5\nelse:\n    if \u00f4 >= m + 0.5: D\n    elif \u00f4 >= m - 1.5: C   (unless dispensability test triggers \u2192 D)\n    else: C if probing (fail_streak <= 2 and near-miss) else D\n```\n\nSelfish core: never cooperate when success is assured or hopeless without me; contribute only when my single endowment is the likely difference between 1 and 1+k; harvest free rides whenever surplus cooperators exist; defect in the final round unless strictly pivotal."

description_SELFISH_8 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Contributor\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely to be pivotal (turning failure into success), otherwise free-ride.\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of opponent cooperators observed in round t (out of n\u22121). Maintain an estimate \u00f4 of expected opponent cooperators, updated after each round:\n- After round t: \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7\u00f4 + 0.4\u00b7o_t (recency-weighted).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 \u2308(n+1)/2\u2309 (threshold plausibly reachable and my vote helps establish success early); otherwise cooperate only if m \u2264 n\u22121 fails narrowly to hold \u2014 i.e., simply: cooperate iff m \u2264 \u23082n/3\u2309. Initialize \u00f4 = o_0 after observing.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (decision rule):**\nLet p = \u00f4 / (n\u22121), predicted opponent cooperators X ~ roughly \u00f4 with spread \u00b11.\n\n1. If \u00f4 \u2265 m + 0.5 (surplus): **Defect** \u2014 threshold met without me; keep the endowment.\n2. If m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 \u00f4 < m + 0.5 (pivotal zone): **Cooperate** \u2014 my contribution likely converts failure (payoff 1) into success (payoff k > 1), so cooperating is selfishly profitable.\n3. If \u00f4 < m \u2212 1.5 (hopeless zone): **Defect** \u2014 my single contribution can't reach the threshold; don't waste the endowment.\n\nRefinement in case 2: cooperate only if k > 1 (always true) AND estimated probability my vote is pivotal, Pr(X = m\u22121) approximated by treating X ~ Binomial(n\u22121, p), satisfies Pr(pivotal)\u00b7k > 1 \u2212 Pr(X \u2265 m)\u00b70 ... in practice: cooperate iff Pr(X = m\u22121) \u00b7 k + Pr(X \u2265 m) \u00b7 0 \u2265 (1 \u2212 something) \u2014 simplified rule: cooperate iff k \u00b7 Pr(X = m\u22121) > 1 \u2212 k\u00b7(indifference); operationally use:\n\n```\np = \u00f4/(n-1)\nP_piv = BinomPMF(m-1; n-1, p)\nif BinomCDF_atLeast(m; n-1, p) > 0.9: Defect      # succeeds anyway\nelif k * P_piv > 1: Cooperate                      # pivotal EV positive\nelif |\u00f4 - (m-1)| <= 1.5: Cooperate                 # near-threshold nudge\nelse: Defect\n```\n\n**Anti-exploitation:** If the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation, switch to Defect for 2 rounds (stop subsidizing a lost cause), then re-test with the rule above.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same one-shot logic, but stricter \u2014 no reputational future to invest in. Defect unless k\u00b7Pr(X = m\u22121) > 1 strictly (i.e., only cooperate when genuinely pivotal in expectation). If \u00f4 \u2265 m, always defect and pocket 1 + k.\n\n**Tie-handling / small n:** If m = n (all must cooperate), cooperate every round while the group has never failed with me cooperating; after any failure, defect for the rest of the game \u2014 the threshold is unrecoverable with defectors present, so keep everything."

description_SELFINTERESTED_1 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Conditional Cooperator**\n\nNotation: let `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t; maintain `est` = expected opponent cooperators for the upcoming round.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1 (threshold plausibly reachable); otherwise cooperate anyway only if k \u2265 2, else defect. (Default: cooperate \u2014 seeding cooperation is cheap relative to k per round.)\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Update `est` as an exponentially weighted average:\n```\nest = 0.6 * coop_others(t-1) + 0.4 * est   (initialize est = coop_others(0) after round 0)\n```\n\nDecision rule each round:\n1. If `est \u2265 m + 1` (threshold comfortably met without me): **Defect** \u2014 free-ride, my contribution isn't pivotal.\n2. If `m - 1.5 \u2264 est < m + 1` (I am plausibly pivotal): **Cooperate** \u2014 my contribution likely swings the outcome, gaining k > 1 at cost 1.\n3. If `est < m - 1.5` (threshold likely fails regardless): **Defect** \u2014 don't waste the endowment. Exception: if this state has persisted fewer than 2 consecutive rounds, cooperate once as a probe/rally attempt, provided last round had at least m - 2 opponent cooperators.\n\n**Failure response:** If the threshold was missed last round *while I cooperated* and `coop_others \u2264 m - 3`, mark opponents as hopeless: defect until a round shows `coop_others \u2265 m - 1`, then resume the rules above.\n\n**Success-exploitation guard:** If I defected under rule 1 and the threshold then failed with exactly m-1 total cooperators (my defection was pivotal), immediately cooperate next round regardless of `est` \u2014 restore the equilibrium I broke.\n\n**Last round (t = r-1):** Same rules, but tighten rule 2 to `m - 1 \u2264 est < m + 0.5`: cooperate only if genuinely pivotal, since there is no future to protect. If `est \u2265 m + 0.5`, defect; if `est < m - 1`, defect.\n\n**Second-to-last round:** Apply normal rules (no early endgame defection \u2014 triggering collapse a round early forfeits k).\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C (unless m > ceil(n/2)+1 and k < 2 \u2192 D)\nelif hopeless_mode: D unless coop_others(t-1) >= m-1 (then exit mode, re-evaluate)\nelif t == r-1:\n    C if m-1 <= est < m+0.5 else D\nelse:\n    if est >= m+1: D\n    elif est >= m-1.5: C\n    else: C once as probe if recent near-miss, else D\n```"

description_SELFINTERESTED_2 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Contributor**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `coop_others(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(2n/3); otherwise defect. (Seed cooperation only when the threshold is plausibly reachable.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let `x = coop_others(t\u22121)` (opponents only, excluding me).\n\n- If `x \u2265 m`: **Defect** \u2014 the threshold is met without me; free-ride.\n- If `x = m \u2212 1`: **Cooperate** \u2014 I am pivotal; paying 1 to gain k (>1) is strictly profitable.\n- If `x = m \u2212 2`: **Cooperate with probability 0.5** \u2014 one other switcher plus me could tip it; probe cheaply. (Deterministic version: cooperate if the threshold was met in any of the last 3 rounds, else defect.)\n- If `x \u2264 m \u2212 3`: **Defect** \u2014 the group is too far from threshold; contribution is likely wasted.\n\n**Failure counter:** Track consecutive rounds where the threshold failed *while I cooperated*. If this reaches 2, defect for the next 2 rounds regardless of x (stop wasting endowment on a hopeless group), then reset and resume the rules above.\n\n**Success-exploitation guard:** If I defected last round and the threshold still failed with x = m\u22121 for two consecutive rounds, cooperate once (opponents may be mirroring me; break the deadlock as pivot).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same pivotality rule: cooperate only if `coop_others(r\u22122) = m \u2212 1` (I'm likely pivotal, and cooperating yields k \u2212 1 > 0 even one-shot); if `x \u2265 m` or `x \u2264 m \u2212 2`, defect.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n: my cooperation is always necessary. Cooperate whenever all n\u22121 opponents cooperated last round; defect otherwise; round 0 cooperate (since k > 1 makes unanimity worth attempting), and apply the 2-failure abandonment rule.\n- If k is very large relative to the deficit (k > m \u2212 x, i.e., even coordinating losses are dwarfed by the prize), shift the x = m\u22122 case to always cooperate.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m <= ceil(2n/3) else D\nif consecutive_wasted_coop >= 2: return D (for 2 rounds, then reset)\nx = opponents_cooperating_last_round\nif x >= m: return D\nif x == m-1: return C\nif x == m-2: return C if threshold_met_within_last_3_rounds else D\nreturn D\n```"

description_SELFINTERESTED_3 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivotal Cooperator**\n\nNotation: at round t, let coop(t\u22121) = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated last round. Maintain a running estimate E = expected opponent cooperators, initialized after round 0 and updated each round as E \u2190 0.5\u00b7E + 0.5\u00b7coop(t\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(n/2 + 1); otherwise defect. (Seed cooperation only when the threshold is plausibly reachable.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (decision rule):** Compare E to m:\n\n1. If coop(t\u22121) \u2265 m (threshold met without me last round): **Defect** \u2014 free-ride, since my contribution was not pivotal.\n2. If coop(t\u22121) = m\u22121 or E \u2208 [m\u22121.5, m\u22120.5): **Cooperate** \u2014 I am likely pivotal; paying 1 to gain k (>1) is profitable.\n3. If coop(t\u22121) = m\u22122 and k \u2265 2: **Cooperate** (gamble on one other marginal cooperator joining, justified by high reward).\n4. Otherwise (E < m\u22122 or hopeless shortfall): **Defect** \u2014 contribution is wasted.\n\nOverride: if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds while I cooperated, defect for the next round regardless (stop subsidizing a lost cause), then re-enter via the rules above.\n\nOverride: if the threshold has succeeded with slack \u2265 2 (coop(t\u22121) \u2265 m+1) for 2 consecutive rounds, defect and continue defecting until slack drops below 1, then resume rules 1\u20134.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same pivotality logic \u2014 cooperate **only** if coop(r\u22122) = m\u22121 exactly (or E rounds to m\u22121); otherwise defect. No reputational future exists, so cooperate only when the immediate expected gain k times the pivot probability exceeds 1; treat coop = m\u22121 as the sole such case.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if (m <= ceil(n/2)+1) else D\nif t == r-1: return C if coop_last == m-1 else D\n\nif coop_last >= m: return D\nif coop_last == m-1: return C\nif coop_last == m-2 and k >= 2 and fail_streak_while_C < 3: return C\nreturn D\n```\n\nTie-handling / edge cases: if m = n, follow rule 2 strictly (cooperate whenever all others cooperated last round, i.e., coop = m\u22121 = n\u22121 is impossible only if someone defected \u2014 then defect until you observe n\u22121 cooperators, which restarts cooperation). If m \u2212 1 > n \u2212 1 is impossible (m \u2264 n guaranteed), no adjustment needed."

description_SELFINTERESTED_4 = "**Strategy: Conditional Pivotal Cooperation**\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of *opponents* (excluding me) who cooperated in round t. Track a running estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of recent o_t (weight 0.6 on last round, 0.4 on prior estimate).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1; otherwise defect. (Initial optimism only when the threshold is plausibly reachable.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Decide based on last round's opponent count o = o_{t\u22121} and estimate \u00f4:\n\n1. **Pivotal zone (o \u2208 {m\u22121, m}):** Cooperate. My contribution is likely decisive: cooperating turns a payoff of 1 into k (gain k\u22121 > 0), or defecting risks dropping the group below threshold.\n2. **Surplus zone (o \u2265 m+1):** Defect. The threshold clears without me; free-ride for 1 + k. Exception: if o = m+1 and o has declined for two consecutive rounds, cooperate (guard against cascade collapse).\n3. **Deficit zone (o \u2264 m\u22122):** Defect by default \u2014 my single contribution can't reach the threshold, so cooperating just loses 1. Exception (rescue probe): if o = m\u22122 and \u00f4 is rising, cooperate once; if the round still fails, do not probe again until o \u2265 m\u22121 is observed.\n\n**Persistent-failure lockout:** If the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds while I cooperated in at least one of them, defect until o_t \u2265 m\u22121 is observed again.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same rules as above but stricter: cooperate only if o_{r\u22121's previous round} \u2208 {m\u22121, m} \u2014 i.e., only when plausibly pivotal. No rescue probes, no anti-cascade cooperation. There is no future to invest in; cooperate solely when the immediate expected gain (probability my vote is decisive \u00d7 k) exceeds the cost of 1, which holds only near the pivot.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C if m <= ceil(n/2)+1 else D\nelse:\n    o = opponents_cooperating(t-1)\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if o in {m-1, m} else D\n    elif lockout_active and o < m-1: play D\n    elif o in {m-1, m}: play C\n    elif o == m+1 and declining_two_rounds: play C\n    elif o == m-2 and o_trend_rising and not probed_recently: play C  # one-shot probe\n    else: play D\n```\n\nThe core logic: contribute only when the contribution likely buys the reward (pivotality), free-ride whenever the group over-supplies, and abandon a group that cannot reach the threshold \u2014 every cooperation must have positive expected private return."

description_SELFINTERESTED_5 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Pivot**\n\nNotation: at the start of round t, let `others_C(t-1)` = number of opponents who cooperated last round. Maintain `fail_streak` = number of consecutive past rounds where the threshold was missed.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if k > 1 (always true) and m \u2264 ceil(n/2 + 1); otherwise cooperate anyway unless m = n (then cooperate too, since success requires everyone). In short: **Cooperate in round 0** to probe and seed coordination.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r-2 (main phase):** Decide based on last round's opponent cooperation count:\n\n1. If `others_C(t-1) \u2265 m`: the threshold was met without needing me \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride; my contribution is pivotal only if others drop to exactly m-1).\n2. If `others_C(t-1) == m - 1`: I am exactly pivotal \u2192 **Cooperate** (my C converts payoff from 1 to 1+k\u22121 = k > 1; strictly profitable if others repeat).\n3. If `others_C(t-1) == m - 2` and I cooperated last round (so total was m-1, one short): **Cooperate** once more, hoping one waverer joins. Track this: if the same situation repeats twice in a row without success, switch to rule 4.\n4. If `others_C(t-1) < m - 2` (hopelessly short): **Defect**.\n\n**Failure cutoff:** If `fail_streak \u2265 3` (threshold missed three consecutive rounds), **Defect** permanently until a round occurs where `others_C \u2265 m - 1`, which resets `fail_streak` to 0 and resumes the main rules.\n\n**Oscillation damping:** If my defection under rule 1 caused a failure last round (i.e., I defected, others_C = m-1, threshold missed), immediately return to cooperating via rule 2 \u2014 do not defect twice in a row when I'm pivotal.\n\n**Last round (t = r-1):** Cooperate only if `others_C(r-2) == m - 1` exactly (I'm pivotal and expected gain k > cost 1). If `others_C(r-2) \u2265 m`, defect and free-ride. Otherwise defect \u2014 no future to invest in.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: play C\nelif t == r-1:\n    play C if others_C(t-1) == m-1 else D\nelse:\n    x = others_C(t-1)\n    if fail_streak >= 3 and x < m-1: play D\n    elif x >= m:\n        if I defected last round and last round failed: play C  # can't happen; safety\n        else: play D\n    elif x == m-1: play C\n    elif x == m-2 and my_last == C and not tried_rescue_twice: play C\n    else: play D\n```\n\nUpdate `fail_streak` each round: increment on failure, reset to 0 on success or when `others_C \u2265 m-1`."

description_SELFINTERESTED_6 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Contributor**\n\nNotation: after each round t, observe o_t = number of opponents (excluding me) who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if k > 1 and m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1; otherwise cooperate anyway unless m = n (then cooperate too, since threshold needs everyone). Concretely: play C in round 0.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (decision for round t based on o_{t\u22121}):**\n\n1. If o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m: enough opponents met the threshold without me last round. Play D (free-ride; the threshold likely holds).\n2. If o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 1: I am pivotal. Play C (my contribution converts payoff from 1 to k, and k > 1).\n3. If o_{t\u22121} = m \u2212 2: play C once as a rescue attempt, but only if I haven't already made a failed rescue in the previous round (i.e., I played C last round and the threshold still failed with total cooperators \u2264 m \u2212 2). Otherwise play D.\n4. If o_{t\u22121} \u2264 m \u2212 3: play D (threshold is out of reach; keep the endowment).\n\n**Recovery rule:** if I defected under rule 1 and the threshold then failed with o_t = m \u2212 1 (my defection broke it), immediately return to C next round and stay in C until rule 1 triggers again.\n\n**Streak-of-failure cutoff:** track consecutive rounds where total cooperators < m. If this streak reaches 3, switch to permanent D until some round shows o_t \u2265 m \u2212 1, which resets the streak and re-enables the rules above.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):**\n- If o_{r\u22122} \u2265 m: play D (free-ride on momentum).\n- If o_{r\u22122} = m \u2212 1: play C (pivotal; C yields k > 1 vs D yielding ~1).\n- Otherwise: play D (no future to invest in, threshold unlikely).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C\no = opponents_cooperated(t-1)\nif failure_streak >= 3 and o < m-1: return D\nif t == r-1:\n    return C if o == m-1 else D\nif o >= m:\n    return D\nif o == m-1:\n    return C\nif o == m-2:\n    return C if not (my_last_action == C and last_total <= m-2) else D\nreturn D\n```"

description_SELFINTERESTED_7 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Pivot**\n\nMaintain after each round t: `others_C(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil(n/2) + 1 (threshold plausibly reachable); otherwise defect. Exception: if m == n, cooperate (only unanimity works, so signal willingness).\n\n**Rounds 1 to r-2:** Base decision on last round's opponent cooperation count `o = others_C(t-1)`:\n\n1. If `o \u2265 m`: threshold met without me \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride; the group succeeds anyway).\n2. If `o == m - 1`: I am pivotal \u2192 **Cooperate** (my C converts my payoff from 1 to 1+k\u22121 = k > 1).\n3. If `o == m - 2`: **Cooperate** with probability 0.5 unless the threshold has failed in the two most recent rounds despite my cooperation in both \u2014 then **Defect**. (Probe: one more riser besides me could tip it.)\n4. If `o \u2264 m - 3`: **Defect** (too far from threshold; contribution is wasted).\n\nAdditional recovery rule: after rule 1 causes a failure (I defected on `o \u2265 m` and then observe `o < m`), treat the next round using the rules above on the new count \u2014 i.e., return to cooperating if pivotal. Never defect twice in a row after a failure where `o == m-1`.\n\nStreak cutoff: track consecutive rounds where I cooperated but the threshold failed. If this counter reaches 3, defect for the remainder except when `o \u2265 m - 1` in the immediately preceding round (reset counter on any success).\n\n**Last round (t = r-1):** Same rules 1\u20134, but tighten rule 3: cooperate only if `o == m - 1` exactly (pure pivotality); defect on `o == m - 2`. No future to invest in \u2014 cooperate only when the single-round return (k > 1 vs. keeping 1) is directly secured by my pivotal contribution based on the best available estimate of others' behavior.\n\n**Special case m == n throughout:** Cooperate as long as all n\u22121 opponents cooperated last round; defect permanently after any observed defection (grim), since success is impossible without unanimity and further contribution is pure loss."

description_SELFINTERESTED_8 = "**Strategy: Conditional Threshold Pivot**\n\nNotation: after each round t, let o_t = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t.\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if the group plausibly needs me: cooperate iff m \u2264 \u2308(n+1)/2\u2309 (threshold reachable with modest turnout); otherwise defect. (Simple default: cooperate if m/n \u2264 0.6, else defect.)\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22121 (except last round rule below):** Use last round's opponent count o = o_{t\u22121}:\n\n1. **If o \u2265 m:** opponents alone met the threshold \u2014 my contribution is superfluous. **Defect** (free-ride).\n2. **If o = m\u22121:** I am pivotal \u2014 my cooperation converts payoff from 1 to 1+k\u22121 = k > 1. **Cooperate.**\n3. **If o = m\u22122:** near-miss; one other player switching plus me could succeed. **Cooperate**, but only if this state hasn't failed twice in a row already; after two consecutive failed rounds with o < m\u22121, defect.\n4. **If o \u2264 m\u22123:** threshold is out of reach \u2014 cooperating just burns endowment. **Defect.**\n\n**Recovery probe:** if defecting due to rule 4 (or the give-up clause in rule 3), cooperate once every \u2308r/5\u2309 rounds as a probe to test whether the group has revived \u2014 but only if at least 3 rounds remain and m \u2264 n\u22121. If the probe round yields o \u2265 m\u22121, resume the rules above normally; otherwise return to defecting.\n\n**Free-rider correction:** if I defected under rule 1 and the round then *failed* (total cooperators < m because I withheld), immediately cooperate next round regardless of o \u2014 my defection was pivotal and cost me k\u22121 net.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** cooperate only if pivotal by best estimate: cooperate iff o_{r\u22122} = m\u22121 (or the free-rider correction triggered). Otherwise defect \u2014 no future to invest in.\n\n**Second-to-last round:** apply normal rules; do not preemptively defect (threshold success still pays k this round).\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m <= ceil((n+1)/2) else D\no = opponents_cooperating(t-1)\nif t == r-1: return C if (o == m-1 or pivotal_fail_flag) else D\nif pivotal_fail_flag: return C          # I broke the threshold last round\nif o >= m:   return D\nif o == m-1: return C\nif o == m-2: return C if consecutive_failures < 2 else probe_or_D\nreturn probe_or_D                        # o <= m-3\n```\n\nwhere `probe_or_D` cooperates on scheduled probe rounds (every \u2308r/5\u2309 rounds, \u22653 rounds remaining), else defects; and `pivotal_fail_flag` is set when I defected, o \u2265 m\u22121... specifically when o = m\u22121 and the round failed only because of my defection."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_1 = "**Strategy: Marginal Pivot Freeriding**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution appears pivotal to reaching the threshold; otherwise defect and freeride on others' cooperation.\n\nNotation: let `others_C[t]` = number of opponents (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Maintain a smoothed forecast of opponent cooperation:\n\n```\nforecast = others_C[0]                     # after round 0\nafter each round t: forecast = 0.6 * others_C[t] + 0.4 * forecast\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Defect if m \u2264 ceil((n\u22121)/2) (plausible the threshold is met without me); cooperate only if m > ceil((n\u22121)/2) and k \u2265 2 (my contribution likely needed and reward outweighs cost); otherwise defect.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Predict opponent cooperators as `p = round(forecast)`.\n\n- If `p \u2265 m`: **Defect** \u2014 threshold likely met without me; take 1 + k.\n- If `p == m \u2212 1`: **Cooperate** \u2014 I'm pivotal; paying 1 to gain k is profitable since k > 1. Exception: if in the last two rounds `others_C` was \u2265 m both times (others are over-supplying), defect once to test whether I'm truly needed; if the threshold then fails, resume cooperating when pivotal.\n- If `p \u2264 m \u2212 2`: **Defect** \u2014 threshold likely fails regardless; don't waste the endowment. Exception: if `p == m \u2212 2` and the last round had exactly m\u22121 or m cooperators total (group is hovering at the edge) and there are at least 3 rounds remaining, cooperate once as a probe to try to establish a threshold-meeting pattern I can later exploit.\n\n**Failure-recovery:** If I cooperated last round but the threshold still failed (`others_C[t] + 1 < m`), defect this round regardless of forecast \u2014 don't repeatedly subsidize a hopeless group. Re-enter cooperation only if `others_C` rises back to exactly m\u22121.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Cooperate only if the forecast says `p == m \u2212 1` exactly (pivotal one-shot gain of k\u22121 > 0); otherwise defect. No reputational concerns remain, so never cooperate speculatively.\n\n**Tie-handling on rounding:** when forecast is exactly halfway, round down (assume fewer cooperators), which biases toward cooperating only when genuinely needed \u2014 but if that rounding yields `p = m\u22121` vs `p = m`, choose defect if `others_C` reached \u2265 m in the most recent round."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_2 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Riding Strategy**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal; free-ride whenever the group appears to reach the threshold without me, and abandon ship when the threshold appears unreachable.\n\nNotation: let `o_t` = number of *other* players who cooperated in round t (observable). Track a forecast `E` of others' cooperators, updated by exponential smoothing:\n```\nE \u2190 o_0 after round 0\nE \u2190 0.6 * o_t + 0.4 * E after each round t\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(n/2) (threshold is easy, seed success and probe); otherwise defect and observe.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Classify the forecast:\n- **Surplus zone** (E \u2265 m + 0.5): others meet the threshold without me \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride on the reward).\n- **Pivotal zone** (m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 E < m + 0.5): my vote plausibly decides the outcome \u2192 **Cooperate**, since k > 1 means paying 1 to secure k is profitable when pivotal.\n- **Hopeless zone** (E < m \u2212 1.5): threshold unlikely even with me \u2192 **Defect** (don't waste the endowment).\n\nExceptions/adjustments:\n- If exactly the pivotal case occurred last round (o_t == m \u2212 1 and I cooperated and threshold met), keep cooperating \u2014 I'm demonstrably load-bearing.\n- If I defected last round and the threshold still succeeded, keep defecting until it fails (ride the surplus as long as it lasts).\n- After a failure caused while I was defecting with o_t == m \u2212 1 (I was the missing cooperator), cooperate next round to restore the reward stream.\n- **Probing:** if I've cooperated in 3 consecutive successful rounds with o_t \u2265 m \u2212 1, defect once to test whether the group succeeds without me. If it succeeds, stay in defect (surplus rule); if it fails, resume cooperation immediately. Don't probe in the last 2 rounds.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** No future to protect, so be maximally selfish: **Cooperate only if strictly pivotal by forecast** \u2014 i.e., E rounds to exactly m \u2212 1 (m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 E < m \u2212 0.5) \u2014 otherwise Defect.\n\n**Failsafe:** if the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation in each, switch to permanent Defect until some round shows o_t \u2265 m \u2212 1, then re-enter the normal rules."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_3 = "**Strategy: \"Marginal Pivot\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal (exactly m cooperators would fail without me); free-ride whenever the group seems likely to hit the threshold without me, or hopeless.\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of *opponent* cooperators observed in round t (0 \u2264 o_t \u2264 n\u22121). Maintain an estimate \u00f4 of opponent cooperation for the next round.\n\n**Estimation:**\n- \u00f4 = exponentially weighted average of opponent cooperators: after each round, \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_t + 0.4\u00b7\u00f4.\n- Also track trend: \u0394 = o_t \u2212 o_{t\u22121}.\n- Predicted opponents next round: p = \u00f4 + 0.5\u00b7\u0394 (clamped to [0, n\u22121]).\n\n**Decision rule (rounds t \u2265 1):**\n- If p \u2265 m: **Defect** (threshold met without me \u2014 free-ride).\n- If p \u2264 m \u2212 2 \u2212 \u03b5, where \u03b5 = max(0, 0.05\u00b7n): **Defect** (hopeless \u2014 my single contribution won't save it; don't waste the endowment).\n- If m \u2212 2 \u2212 \u03b5 < p < m: **Cooperate** (I am plausibly pivotal; the reward k > 1 exceeds my cost of 1).\n\nConcretely: cooperate iff m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 p < m (using p rounded pivotality band); otherwise defect.\n\n**First round (t = 0):**\nNo information. Assume opponents cooperate independently with probability q\u2080 = m/n. Expected opponent cooperators = (n\u22121)\u00b7m/n.\n- If (n\u22121)\u00b7m/n \u2265 m: Defect (likely met without me).\n- Else: Cooperate iff m \u2264 (n\u22121)\u00b7m/n + 1.5 (i.e., plausibly pivotal); otherwise Defect. In practice: cooperate in round 0 only when m/n > (n\u22121)/n\u00b7(m/n) leaves a gap of at most ~1.5, which typically means cooperate when m is large relative to n (m/n \u2265 0.5), defect otherwise.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):**\nSame pivotality rule \u2014 no future to protect, so be strictly opportunistic: defect unless p is in [m\u22121, m), i.e., you appear exactly pivotal. Tighten the band: cooperate only if m \u2212 1 \u2264 p < m.\n\n**Anti-exploitation guard:**\nIf I cooperated and the threshold still failed in 2 consecutive rounds, defect for the next 2 rounds (stop subsidizing a losing group), then resume normal rule.\n\n**Sucker-check guard:**\nIf the threshold has succeeded in the last 3 rounds while I defected each time, keep defecting (free-riding is working \u2014 don't fix what isn't broken).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\no_hist = []; \u00f4 = (n-1)*m/n\nfor t in 0..r-1:\n    if t == 0:\n        action = C if (m - \u00f4) in (0, 1.5] else D\n    else:\n        \u0394 = o_hist[-1] - (o_hist[-2] if t>1 else o_hist[-1])\n        p = clamp(\u00f4 + 0.5*\u0394, 0, n-1)\n        band_low = m - 1 if t == r-1 else m - 1.5\n        if guard_active(): action = D\n        elif band_low <= p < m: action = C\n        else: action = D\n    play(action); observe o_t\n    \u00f4 = 0.6*o_t + 0.4*\u00f4; o_hist.append(o_t)\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_4 = "**Strategy: Marginal Pivot Freerider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal (exactly m-1 others expected to cooperate); defect whenever the threshold looks safe without me or hopeless.\n\n**State tracked:** For each opponent-cooperation count observed, keep a recency-weighted estimate \u0108 of the number of opponents who will cooperate next round:\n- After round t, update \u0108 \u2190 0.6 \u00b7 (observed opponent cooperators in t) + 0.4 \u00b7 \u0108.\n\n**Decision rule (round t):**\nLet E = round(\u0108) = expected opponent cooperators.\n\n1. If E \u2265 m: **Defect** (threshold met without me; freeride).\n2. If E == m \u2212 1: **Cooperate** (I'm pivotal; gain k > 1 by contributing, since k \u2212 0 > 1 \u2212 ... actually payoff C-pivotal = k vs D = 1, and k > 1).\n3. If E \u2264 m \u2212 2: **Defect** (my single contribution can't reach the threshold; don't waste the endowment) \u2014 with one exception below.\n\n**Exception \u2014 probe when close:** If E == m \u2212 2 and the threshold was met in at least one of the last two rounds, cooperate with probability 0.5 (others may be conditional cooperators who return if success looks possible). Otherwise defect.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- **First round (t=0):** No data. Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(n/2) (thresholds a random-ish population plausibly nears, and being pivotal early trains reciprocators); otherwise defect. Initialize \u0108 to the observed count after round 0.\n- **Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same rule but stricter: cooperate only if E == m \u2212 1 exactly (no probing exception) \u2014 pure pivotality, since no future to invest in.\n- **Second-to-last round:** Apply the normal rule (still worth keeping conditional cooperators engaged for the final round's threshold).\n- **Ties/noise:** If the last two observed counts differ by \u2265 2 (volatile opponents), use min of the two counts as E instead of the smoothed estimate \u2014 err toward cooperating only when clearly pivotal.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nif t == 0: play C if m <= ceil(n/2) else D\nelse:\n    E = round(Chat)  # or min(last two counts) if volatile\n    if E >= m: play D\n    elif E == m-1: play C\n    elif E == m-2 and t < r-1 and threshold_met_recently: play C w.p. 0.5\n    else: play D\nupdate Chat after observing round outcome\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_5 = "**Strategy: Marginal Pivot Freerider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal to hitting the threshold; otherwise keep the endowment and free-ride on others' cooperation.\n\nNotation: after each round t, record o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated. Maintain an estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of others' cooperation, weighting recent rounds more:\n\u00f4 = (2\u00b7o_{t-1} + o_{t-2}) / 3 (use o_{t-1} alone if only one round observed).\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(n/2) and k \u2265 2 (threshold plausibly reachable and reward worth the gamble); otherwise defect.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (decision rule):**\n1. If \u00f4 \u2265 m: others alone likely meet the threshold \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride).\n2. If \u00f4 = m \u2212 1 (i.e., m\u22121 \u2264 \u00f4 < m): I am likely pivotal \u2192 **Cooperate** (payoff k > cost 1).\n3. If \u00f4 < m \u2212 1: threshold likely fails even with me \u2192 **Defect** (don't waste the endowment), with one exception:\n   - *Rescue probe:* if \u00f4 \u2265 m \u2212 2 and last round's failure was by exactly one or two cooperators, cooperate with probability 0.5 for one round to try to tip a near-miss coordination upward. Never probe two rounds in a row after failure.\n4. Hysteresis against exploitation of my pivotality: if I have cooperated in the last 3 consecutive rounds while o_t stayed exactly at m\u22121 (others parked me on the pivot), defect once to force others to pick up the slack, then resume the rule.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same rules but stricter: defect unless \u00f4 is exactly in [m\u22121, m) \u2014 cooperate only if pivotal is very likely (o_{r-2} == m\u22121 exactly). No rescue probes; no reason to invest in future coordination.\n\n**Special cases:**\n- If m = n: my cooperation is always necessary. Cooperate as long as o_{t-1} = n\u22121 (unanimity held); permanently defect after any observed defection by others.\n- If success has occurred in \u2265 3 consecutive rounds while I defected, keep defecting (stable free ride) until a failure occurs, then re-evaluate via the rules above.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if (m <= ceil(n/2) and k >= 2) else D\nif m == n: return C if all previous rounds had o = n-1 else D\n\u00f4 = weighted_avg(o history)\nif t == r-1: return C if o_{t-1} == m-1 else D\nif \u00f4 >= m: return D\nif m-1 <= \u00f4 < m:\n    if cooperated last 3 rounds and o stuck at m-1: return D  # squeeze test\n    return C\nif \u00f4 >= m-2 and last round failed by \u22642 and not probed last round:\n    return C with prob 0.5\nreturn D\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_6 = "**Strategy: Marginal Pivot Free-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my own contribution is likely pivotal to reaching the threshold; otherwise free-ride on others' cooperation or abandon a lost cause.\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of *opponents* (out of n\u22121) who cooperated in round t. Maintain an estimate of expected opponent cooperators:\n\n- \u00f4 = o_{t-1} if only one round observed\n- Otherwise \u00f4 = 0.6\u00b7o_{t-1} + 0.4\u00b7o_{t-2} (recency-weighted)\n\n**Decision rule for round t \u2265 1:**\n\n1. If \u00f4 \u2265 m + 0.5: play **D** (threshold safely met without me \u2014 free-ride).\n2. If m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 \u00f4 < m + 0.5: play **C** (I am plausibly pivotal; my 1 unit buys k > 1).\n3. If \u00f4 < m \u2212 1.5: play **D** (threshold likely fails regardless; don't waste the endowment), **except**: if \u00f4 \u2265 m \u2212 2.5 and the group succeeded in at least half of past rounds, play C (rescue attempt when history shows the group is capable).\n\n**First round (t = 0):**\n- If m \u2264 ceil((n\u22121)/2): play **D** \u2014 decent chance others alone hit the threshold, so probe by free-riding.\n- Otherwise play **C** \u2014 a demanding threshold needs my contribution to have any chance, and success is worth k.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):**\n- Play **C** only if exactly pivotal is plausible: m \u2212 1.5 \u2264 \u00f4 < m \u2212 0.5 (i.e., opponents expected to fall exactly one short). Otherwise **D** \u2014 no future to invest in; defect whenever the threshold will be met or missed without me.\n\n**Second-to-last round:** apply the normal rule but drop the rescue exception in step 3 (no time for signaling to pay off).\n\n**Tie-breaking / noise handling:** if o has oscillated (|o_{t-1} \u2212 o_{t-2}| \u2265 2), treat \u00f4 as the minimum of the two observations for the free-ride test in step 1 (only free-ride when success without me is robust), and as the maximum for the abandonment test in step 3 (only abandon when failure is robust). When in doubt between C and D under these adjusted bounds, play C \u2014 a spent endowment costs 1, a missed threshold costs k > 1.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m > ceil((n-1)/2) else D\n\u00f4 = weighted estimate of opponent cooperators\nif t == r-1:\n    return C if m-1.5 <= \u00f4 < m-0.5 else D\nif \u00f4 >= m + 0.5: return D            # free-ride\nif \u00f4 >= m - 1.5: return C            # pivotal\nif \u00f4 >= m - 2.5 and success_rate >= 0.5 and t < r-2:\n    return C                          # rescue\nreturn D                              # lost cause\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_7 = "**Strategy: \"Marginal Pivoter\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal \u2014 i.e., when the expected number of other cooperators is close to m\u22121. Otherwise free-ride (either the threshold is safe without me, or hopeless with me).\n\n**State tracked:**\n- For each past round t: o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated.\n- Estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of others' cooperation, weighting recent rounds more: \u00f4 = \u03a3 w_t\u00b7o_t / \u03a3 w_t with w_t = 0.7^(age). Also track s = sample standard deviation of o_t over the last min(3, rounds played) rounds (use 1 if fewer than 2 observations).\n\n**Decision rule (rounds t \u2265 1):**\n1. If \u00f4 \u2265 m \u2212 1 + max(1, s): DEFECT (threshold likely met without me \u2014 free-ride).\n2. Else if \u00f4 < m \u2212 1 \u2212 max(1, s): DEFECT (hopeless \u2014 don't waste contribution), **except** apply a probe: if the threshold has never been met and t < r\u22121, cooperate with probability 0.2 to test whether others can be rallied.\n3. Else (\u00f4 within \u00b1max(1,s) of m\u22121): COOPERATE \u2014 I'm plausibly pivotal, and payoff k > 1 = cost, so pivotal cooperation pays.\n\n**Refinement for rule 3 (opportunistic shaving):** if the threshold was met in each of the last 2 rounds AND o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m (it was met even ignoring my contribution), DEFECT once to test whether others carry the load. If the threshold then fails, return to cooperating under rule 3.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- **Round 0:** No data. Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil(n/2) (threshold cheap enough that a coalition likely forms and my contribution helps seed it); otherwise defect and observe.\n- **Last round (t = r\u22121):** No future to influence, but the round payoff logic is identical (pivotal cooperation still yields k > 1). Apply rules 1\u20133 but disable the probe in rule 2 and tighten the pivot band: cooperate only if m \u2212 1 \u2212 s \u2264 \u00f4 \u2264 m \u2212 1 + 0.5 (be more willing to gamble that others cover the last slot).\n- **Second-to-last round:** Disable the shaving test (no time to recover from a failed threshold cascade).\n- **Ties/exact values:** treat boundaries as written (\u2265 / <).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m <= ceil(n/2) else D\ncompute \u00f4, s; band = max(1, s)\nif t == r-1: band_hi = 0.5 else band_hi = band\nif \u00f4 >= m-1 + band_hi: return D\nif \u00f4 < m-1 - band:\n    if never_met and t < r-1: return C with prob 0.2 else D\n    return D\n# pivotal zone\nif t < r-2 and met_last_two_rounds and o_{t-1} >= m and not shaved_last_round:\n    return D  # shave test\nreturn C\n```"

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_8 = "**Opportunistic Threshold-Riding Strategy**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution is likely pivotal to hitting the threshold; free-ride whenever the group seems likely to succeed without me or to fail regardless.\n\nNotation: at end of each round observe `others_C(t)` = number of opponents who cooperated (out of n\u22121). Track a running forecast of opponent cooperation:\n\n```\nforecast = weighted average of others_C over history,\n           weight recent rounds more (e.g., EWMA with \u03b1 = 0.6)\n```\n\n**Round 0 (no history):**\n- If m \u2264 n/2, defect (good odds enough others cover it, or it fails anyway \u2014 either way keeping the endowment is best).\n- Else cooperate (threshold is demanding; seed success so there's surplus to exploit later).\n\n**Rounds 1 \u2026 r\u22122 (decision rule):**\nLet `E = forecast` of opponents cooperating this round.\n- If E \u2265 m: **Defect** \u2014 threshold met without me; pocket 1 + k.\n- If E \u2264 m \u2212 2: **Defect** \u2014 my contribution can't save it; don't waste the endowment. Exception: if E \u2265 m \u2212 2 and last round's `others_C` was volatile (|others_C(t\u22121) \u2212 others_C(t\u22122)| \u2265 2) and k \u2265 2, cooperate to gamble on being pivotal, since k > 1 makes a successful pivotal contribution profitable.\n- If m \u2212 2 < E < m (i.e., E in the pivotal window, roughly E \u2208 [m\u22121, m)): **Cooperate** \u2014 my single vote plausibly tips the outcome, and payoff k > 1 exceeds the kept endowment.\n\nTie-breaking / hysteresis: if I defected last round and the threshold failed by exactly 1 (total cooperators = m\u22121), cooperate this round \u2014 I was the missing pivot. If I cooperated last round and total cooperators \u2265 m+1, defect this round \u2014 my contribution was redundant.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):**\nApply the same pivotal rule but tighten: cooperate only if forecast is exactly in [m\u22121, m) \u2014 i.e., I'm very likely pivotal. Otherwise defect, since there's no future to protect and no retaliation possible.\n\n**Exploitation escalation:** if the threshold has been met in \u2265 3 consecutive rounds with total cooperators \u2265 m+1, defect regardless of forecast until a failure or a round with cooperators = m occurs \u2014 ride the surplus as long as it lasts.\n\n**Collapse handling:** if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds and my cooperation didn't change outcomes, lock into permanent defection unless `others_C` jumps to \u2265 m\u22121, in which case re-enter the pivotal rule.\n\n```\ndef act(t, history):\n    if t == 0: return C if m > n/2 else D\n    E = ewma(others_C history, \u03b1=0.6)\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C if m-1 <= E < m else D\n    if exploit_streak >= 3: return D\n    if collapse and last_others_C < m-1: return D\n    if E >= m: return D\n    if m-1 <= E < m: return C\n    if last_total == m-1 and my_last == D: return C\n    return D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_1 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Free-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution is likely to be the difference between missing and meeting the threshold; otherwise defect and free-ride on the reward.\n\nNotation: after each round t, record o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (0 \u2264 o_t \u2264 n\u22121).\n\n**Round 0:** Defect. (No information; keep the endowment and probe the field.)\n\n**Rounds t \u2265 1:** Form an estimate \u00f4 of others' cooperation this round:\n- \u00f4 = 0.7 \u00b7 o_{t\u22121} + 0.3 \u00b7 (mean of all previous o's)  (rounded to nearest integer).\n\nDecision rule:\n1. If \u00f4 \u2265 m: defect \u2014 the threshold is expected to be met without me; my C would only cost 1 for nothing extra.\n2. If \u00f4 = m \u2212 1: cooperate \u2014 I am pivotal; paying 1 to gain k (>1) is profitable.\n3. If \u00f4 = m \u2212 2 and last round's o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m \u2212 2 and round-to-round variance in o is high (o has fluctuated by \u22651 between recent rounds): cooperate \u2014 a wobble upward plus my contribution can secure k.\n4. If \u00f4 \u2264 m \u2212 2 otherwise: defect \u2014 the group is too far from the threshold; contributing is a wasted endowment.\n\n**Tie-breaking / instability handling:** If in the previous round o_{t\u22121} was exactly m \u2212 1 and I defected (threshold missed by one), cooperate this round regardless of \u00f4 \u2014 my defection likely caused the failure, and being pivotal pays.\n\nIf I cooperated last round and the total cooperators (including me) exceeded m by 2 or more, defect this round \u2014 I was superfluous; test whether others carry the threshold.\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Same rule, but only cooperate in the strictly pivotal case (rule 2, \u00f4 = m \u2212 1). No investment in stability or signaling since there is no future.\n\n**Penultimate rounds:** No special treatment \u2014 the rule is already myopically self-interested each round.\n\nPseudocode:\n\n```\nif t == 0: play D\nelse:\n    \u00f4 = round(0.7*o[t-1] + 0.3*mean(o[0..t-1]))\n    if t == r-1:\n        play C if \u00f4 == m-1 else D\n    elif o[t-1] == m-1 and my_last == D:\n        play C\n    elif my_last == C and (o[t-1]+1) >= m+2:\n        play D\n    elif \u00f4 >= m: play D\n    elif \u00f4 == m-1: play C\n    elif \u00f4 == m-2 and volatile(o): play C\n    else: play D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_2 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Freerider\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal to reaching the threshold; otherwise defect and free-ride on others' cooperation.\n\n**Notation:** After each round t, observe o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated. Maintain an exponentially smoothed estimate of others' cooperation:\n- \u00f4 \u2190 o_0 after round 0; thereafter \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_t + 0.4\u00b7\u00f4.\n\n**Round 0 (no history):**\n- Cooperate iff (m \u2212 1)/(n \u2212 1) \u2265 0.5 is false... simply: if m/n \u2264 0.5, defect (likely enough cooperators without me); otherwise cooperate (help establish the threshold, since expected value k > 1 makes success worth one endowment).\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122 (main rule):** Predict others' cooperators p = round(\u00f4).\n- If p \u2265 m: **Defect** \u2014 threshold expected without me; free-ride.\n- If p == m \u2212 1: **Cooperate** \u2014 I am pivotal; paying 1 to gain k (>1) is profitable.\n- If p \u2264 m \u2212 2: **Defect** by default (contribution wasted), **except**: if p == m \u2212 2 and last round's o_t showed an upward trend (o_t > o_{t\u22121}) or o_t == m \u2212 1, cooperate once as a probe. If a probe fails (threshold missed), don't probe again until o_t \u2265 m \u2212 2 for two consecutive rounds.\n\n**Collapse detection:** If the threshold has been missed in the last 3 consecutive rounds and \u00f4 < m \u2212 2, defect for all remaining rounds (group is hopeless; keep endowments).\n\n**Last round (t = r \u2212 1):** Same pivotal logic, but stricter \u2014 cooperate **only if** p == m \u2212 1 exactly (i.e., \u00f4 rounds to m \u2212 1). Otherwise defect: no future to invest in, so only pay when immediately pivotal.\n\n**Tie/edge handling:**\n- If m \u2212 1 == n \u2212 1 (everyone needed): cooperate every round until the threshold has ever been missed once; after any miss, defect forever.\n- If \u00f4 is exactly between values, round toward m \u2212 1 (bias toward assuming pivotality only when evidence supports it \u2014 i.e., round down if \u00f4 > m \u2212 1, round up if \u00f4 < m \u2212 1 requires it; concretely, p = round(\u00f4) with ties going to the value farther from m, favoring defection).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m/n > 0.5 else D\nif collapsed(): return D\np = round(\u00f4)\nif t == r-1: return C if p == m-1 else D\nif p >= m: return D\nif p == m-1: return C\nif p == m-2 and (rising_trend or probe_allowed): return C\nreturn D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_3 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Freeriding**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution plausibly makes the difference between missing and meeting the threshold; otherwise keep the endowment and freeride on the reward.\n\nNotation: let `others_C(t)` = number of opponents (excluding me) who cooperated in round t. Track a running estimate of expected opponent cooperation:\n\n```\nest = EWMA of others_C with weight 0.6 on most recent round\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate iff m \u2264 ceil((n-1)/2) + 1 (i.e., the threshold is easy enough that a modest coalition plus me likely clears it). Otherwise defect. Exception: if k \u2264 1 + 1/r behave more conservatively \u2014 defect unless m \u2264 n/3.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r-2:** After observing history, decide:\n\n```\nif est >= m:\n    Defect        # threshold likely met without me \u2014 freeride\nelif est >= m - 1.5:\n    Cooperate     # I am plausibly pivotal\nelif est >= m - 3 and k >= 2:\n    Cooperate     # gamble: high reward justifies stretching\nelse:\n    Defect        # threshold hopeless \u2014 don't waste endowment\n```\n\nAdditional overrides:\n- **Success-without-me rule:** if in the previous round the threshold was met and `others_C \u2265 m`, defect this round (test whether I'm needed).\n- **Wasted-contribution rule:** if I cooperated last round and the threshold still failed by 2 or more (total cooperators \u2264 m - 2), defect this round regardless of est.\n- **Re-entry:** if I defected and the threshold failed by exactly 1 (total cooperators = m - 1), cooperate next round \u2014 my single switch would have secured k.\n- **Hopeless lock:** if the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds with total cooperators < m - 2 each time, defect for all remaining rounds.\n\n**Last round (t = r-1):** No future to influence; cooperate only if strictly pivotal in expectation: cooperate iff m - 2 \u2264 est < m and k > 1. Otherwise defect.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- If m = n: my cooperation is always necessary; cooperate every round until the threshold fails once, then defect forever (someone else broke it; further contribution is wasted). Cooperate in round 0.\n- If n - m is large (m \u2264 n/3): start defecting; only cooperate via the pivotal rules above, since others likely cover the threshold.\n- If est data is noisy (opponent cooperation varies by \u2265 3 between rounds), widen the pivotal band to `m - 2.5 \u2264 est < m + 0.5` and cooperate within it, since volatility raises the chance my vote matters."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_4 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Freerider\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my contribution is likely pivotal for reaching the threshold; otherwise keep the endowment and free-ride on others' cooperation.\n\n**State tracked:** For each past round t, o_t = number of *other* players who cooperated (0 to n\u22121). Maintain an estimate \u00f4 = weighted average of o_t with decay: \u00f4 \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_last + 0.4\u00b7\u00f4.\n\n**Decision rule (each round):**\n\n1. **Estimate others' cooperation** \u00f4 as above.\n2. Classify:\n   - **Surplus** (\u00f4 \u2265 m + 0.5): threshold will likely be met without me \u2192 **Defect** (free-ride).\n   - **Hopeless** (\u00f4 \u2264 m \u2212 2): even with my contribution, threshold likely fails \u2192 **Defect** (don't waste endowment).\n   - **Pivotal zone** (m \u2212 2 < \u00f4 < m + 0.5): my contribution plausibly decides success \u2192 **Cooperate**, since k > 1 means securing the reward outweighs the cost of 1.\n\n**Round 0 (no history):** Cooperate if m/n \u2264 2/3 (threshold plausibly reachable and my vote may matter), otherwise defect. Initialize \u00f4 = m (optimistic prior in pivotal zone).\n\n**Hysteresis / anti-oscillation:** If I defected last round for \"surplus\" reasons and the threshold then *failed* with exactly m\u22121 cooperators, immediately cooperate this round (I was likely pivotal).\n\n**Endgame:** In the final round, apply the same rule but tighten the pivotal zone: cooperate only if o_last \u2208 {m\u22121, m} exactly (others may defect in the last round, so require strong evidence I'm pivotal). Never cooperate in the final round if o_last \u2265 m+1 or \u2264 m\u22122.\n\n**Persistent failure cutoff:** If the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation, switch to Defect until a round occurs where o_t \u2265 m\u22121, then re-enter the normal rule.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nif t == 0: return C if m/n <= 2/3 else D\n\u00f4 = 0.6*o_{t-1} + 0.4*\u00f4_prev\nif failed_with_my_C_streak >= 3 and o_{t-1} < m-1: return D\nif last round: return C if o_{t-1} in {m-1, m} else D\nif defected_last and coop_last_total == m-1: return C\nif m - 2 < \u00f4 < m + 0.5: return C\nreturn D\n```\n\nEvery decision maximizes my own expected payoff: pay the contribution cost only when it likely buys me the reward k > 1; otherwise pocket the endowment."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_5 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Freeloader**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution plausibly makes the difference between the threshold failing and succeeding; otherwise keep the endowment and free-ride on any surplus of cooperators.\n\n**State tracked:** for each past round t, the number of *other* players who cooperated, o_t. Maintain a prediction p of others' cooperation this round.\n\n**Prediction:** p = weighted average of recent o_t, weighting recent rounds more (e.g., exponential smoothing: p \u2190 0.6\u00b7o_{t-1} + 0.4\u00b7p). Also track variability: let hits = fraction of past rounds where o_t \u2265 m (others alone met threshold) and pivots = fraction where o_t = m \u2212 1.\n\n**Decision rule each round:**\n1. Compute expected others' cooperators p.\n2. Defect if p \u2265 m (others will likely hit threshold without me \u2014 take 1 + k).\n3. Defect if p \u2264 m \u2212 2 (threshold likely fails even with me \u2014 don't waste the endowment). Exception: if p is within 1 of m \u2212 1 and k \u2265 2, cooperate anyway (cheap insurance since k > 1 means reward outweighs contribution).\n4. Cooperate if m \u2212 2 < p < m (I'm plausibly pivotal: contributing turns ~0 into k, gaining k \u2212 1 > 0).\n\nConcretely: cooperate iff m \u2212 1 \u2212 \u03b4 \u2264 p < m, where \u03b4 = 1 if k \u2265 2, else \u03b4 = 0.5.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- **Round 0:** no data. Cooperate iff my contribution is plausibly pivotal under uniform priors: cooperate if (m \u2212 1)/(n \u2212 1) \u2265 0.4 and k \u2265 1.5; otherwise defect. (Roughly: cooperate when the threshold is demanding relative to group size, defect when others likely cover it.)\n- **Last round:** same rule \u2014 no reputation exists (anonymous), and cooperation here is still individually rational only if pivotal, so apply the standard pivotality rule with a slightly stricter band (\u03b4 = 0): cooperate only if p \u2208 [m \u2212 1, m).\n- **Threshold met without me last round (o_{t-1} \u2265 m):** defect this round (probe for free-riding), but if the threshold then fails and o drops to exactly m \u2212 1, resume cooperating immediately.\n- **Persistent failure:** if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation (o_t < m \u2212 1 each time), switch to permanent defection until some round shows o_t \u2265 m \u2212 1 again \u2014 stop subsidizing a lost cause.\n- **Oscillation guard:** if my defection after a success caused failure (o dropped from \u2265 m to m \u2212 1), lock in cooperation for the next 2 rounds before probing again, to stabilize the profitable equilibrium of exactly-m cooperators including me.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n\n```\np = None\nfailStreakWithMyC = 0\nlockC = 0\n\neach round t:\n    if t == 0:\n        act = C if ((m-1)/(n-1) >= 0.4 and k >= 1.5) else D\n    else:\n        p = 0.6*o_prev + 0.4*(p if p != None else o_prev)\n        delta = 1 if k >= 2 else 0.5\n        if t == r-1: delta = 0\n        if lockC > 0: act = C; lockC -= 1\n        elif failStreakWithMyC >= 3 and o_prev < m-1: act = D\n        elif p >= m: act = D\n        elif p >= m-1-delta: act = C\n        else: act = D\n    play act\n    observe o_t\n    if act==C and o_t + 1 < m: failStreakWithMyC += 1\n    elif o_t + 1 >= m or o_t >= m-1: failStreakWithMyC = 0\n    if act==D and o_prev_success and o_t == m-1: lockC = 2\n```\n\nI contribute only to buy the reward for myself when my vote is the deciding one, exploit any excess cooperation by defecting, and cut losses immediately when the group can't reach the threshold even with my help."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_6 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Free-Rider\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution plausibly decides whether the threshold is met; otherwise defect and free-ride.\n\nNotation: let `coop_prev` = number of *other* players who cooperated last round; keep an exponentially weighted estimate of others' cooperation:\n\n```\nest = coop_prev                     # after round 0\nest = 0.6 * coop_prev + 0.4 * est   # updated each round\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil(n/2) and k \u2265 2 (cheap threshold, high reward \u2014 worth probing); otherwise defect.\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Let g = m \u2212 est (gap without me).\n- If g \u2264 0: **Defect** \u2014 the threshold is likely met without me; free-ride.\n- If 0 < g \u2264 1.5: **Cooperate** \u2014 I am plausibly pivotal, and k > 1 means securing the reward beats keeping my endowment.\n- If g > 1.5: **Defect** \u2014 the threshold is likely lost regardless; don't waste the endowment.\n\nAdjustment for volatility: track whether the threshold was met each round. If it was met in the last round but g \u2264 0 by less than 0.5 (i.e., est is barely at m), cooperate with probability 0.5 to hedge against simultaneous free-riding collapse \u2014 implement deterministically as: cooperate on even-indexed rounds, defect on odd ones, when 0 \u2264 est \u2212 m < 0.5.\n\nCollapse detection: if the threshold has failed for 3 consecutive rounds AND est < m \u2212 2, switch to permanent defection (the group is unrecoverable; keep every endowment).\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Apply the same pivotal rule but tighten the band: cooperate only if 0 < g \u2264 1 (strictly pivotal). If g \u2264 0, defect to capture the maximum payoff 1 + k.\n\n**Edge parameters:**\n- If m = n: cooperate in round 0; thereafter cooperate only if all others cooperated last round, else defect forever.\n- If k is very large (k > n): widen the pivotal band to g \u2264 2.5 in middle rounds, since even a low-probability threshold save dominates the kept endowment."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_7 = "**Strategy: Pivotal Free-Rider**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution is likely to be pivotal in reaching the threshold; otherwise keep my endowment and free-ride on the group's success or accept failure.\n\nNotation: let o_t = number of opposing cooperators observed in round t (out of n\u22121). Maintain a forecast \u00d4 of opposing cooperators, updated as an exponential moving average:\n\n- \u00d4\u2080 = m \u2212 1 (optimistic prior that others are near threshold)\n- After each round: \u00d4 \u2190 0.6 \u00b7 o_t + 0.4 \u00b7 \u00d4\n\n**Decision rule each round t:**\n\n1. Compute the gap g = m \u2212 \u00d4 (how many cooperators are \"missing\" without me).\n2. Cooperate iff 0 < g \u2264 1 + tol, where tol = 0.5 \u2014 i.e., the group is expected to fall just short and my one contribution plausibly tips it.\n3. Defect if g \u2264 0 (threshold likely met without me \u2014 free-ride) or g > 1 + tol (threshold likely out of reach even with me \u2014 don't waste the endowment).\n\n**Overrides and edge cases:**\n\n- Round 0: cooperate iff k > n/m (high stakes relative to group size); otherwise defect to probe.\n- Exact-pivot memory: if in the previous round exactly m\u22121 opponents cooperated and the threshold failed (or exactly m\u22121 opponents cooperated and I cooperated to make it succeed), cooperate this round regardless of \u00d4 \u2014 my vote is demonstrably pivotal.\n- Overshoot memory: if the previous round succeeded with o_{t\u22121} \u2265 m (threshold met without my help), defect this round regardless of \u00d4.\n- Dead-group cutoff: if the threshold has failed in 3 consecutive rounds despite my cooperation, defect for the rest of the game unless o_t rises to \u2265 m\u22121 again (then resume the normal rule).\n- Last round (t = r\u22121): apply the same rule but tighten tol to 0.25 \u2014 cooperate only if very confident I'm pivotal, since there's no future to invest in; if \u00d4 \u2265 m, defect and pocket 1 + k.\n- Trivial case m = 1... excluded by rules, but if effectively my cooperation alone suffices (g \u2264 1 always and k > 1), the pivot rule already handles it: cooperate when no one else will.\n\n```\ndef act(t, history):\n    if t == 0: return C if k > n/m else D\n    o_prev = history[t-1].opp_cooperators\n    update \u00d4\n    if o_prev >= m: return D                 # they don't need me\n    if o_prev == m-1: return C               # I'm pivotal\n    if fail_streak_with_my_C >= 3 and o_prev < m-1: return D\n    g = m - \u00d4\n    tol = 0.25 if t == r-1 else 0.5\n    return C if 0 < g <= 1 + tol else D\n```"

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_8 = "**Strategy: \"Pivotal Freeloader\"**\n\nCore idea: cooperate only when my single contribution plausibly decides whether the threshold is met; otherwise keep the endowment and free-ride on the reward.\n\nNotation: let coop\u208b\u1d62(t) = number of opponents who cooperated in round t (observed after the round). Maintain a forecast E of expected opponent cooperators, updated as an exponential moving average:\n\n```\nE \u2190 coop\u208b\u1d62(0) after round 0\nE \u2190 0.6 * coop\u208b\u1d62(t) + 0.4 * E after each later round\n```\n\n**Round 0:** Cooperate if m \u2264 ceil(n/2) and k \u2265 1.5 (threshold likely reachable and reward worth the gamble); otherwise defect. Exception: if m = n, cooperate (only unanimous cooperation can ever pay, and my defection guarantees failure).\n\n**Rounds 1 to r\u22122:** Predict opponent cooperators as p = round(E). Decide:\n\n- If p \u2265 m: **Defect** \u2014 threshold met without me; pocket 1 + k.\n- If p = m \u2212 1: **Cooperate** \u2014 I'm pivotal; paying 1 to gain k is profitable since k > 1.\n- If p \u2264 m \u2212 2: **Defect** \u2014 my contribution is wasted; the threshold fails regardless.\n\nAnti-lock-in probe: if p \u2264 m \u2212 2 has held for 3 consecutive rounds and coop\u208b\u1d62 in the last round was exactly m \u2212 2 (i.e., group is one opponent short beyond me), cooperate once every 3rd such round to test whether cooperation can be reignited \u2014 but only if remaining rounds \u2265 3 (enough time to recoup the probe cost).\n\nBorderline noise handling: if the fractional part of E is between 0.35 and 0.65 and p would be m or m\u22121, treat it as p = m \u2212 1 (cooperate) \u2014 cheap insurance against near-miss failures, since losing k costs more than the 1 contributed.\n\nSpecial case m = n: cooperate every round as long as all opponents cooperated in the previous round; permanently defect after any opponent defection (grim trigger), since success is then unattainable without full compliance.\n\n**Last round (t = r\u22121):** Same pivotal rule, but stricter: cooperate only if p = m \u2212 1 exactly (no probing, no borderline insurance on the p = m side). If p \u2265 m or p \u2264 m \u2212 2, defect \u2014 there is no future to invest in.\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- m = 2: pivotal only when exactly one opponent is expected to cooperate; follow the general rule.\n- If observed cooperation is highly volatile (last-round count differs from E by \u2265 2), fall back to the raw last-round count instead of E for the prediction."
